1
00:04:56,590 --> 00:04:57,640
No!

2
00:05:31,290 --> 00:05:33,550
There she is. There she is.

3
00:05:42,860 --> 00:05:44,390
There she is.

4
00:14:33,060 --> 00:14:35,050
   Ladies and gentlemen,

5
00:14:35,200 --> 00:14:39,330
   I've traveled over half our state to be here tonight.

6
00:14:39,430 --> 00:14:41,960
   I couldn't get away sooner because my new well was coming in

7
00:14:42,070 --> 00:14:44,970
   at Coyote Hills and I had to see about it.

8
00:14:45,070 --> 00:14:48,070
   That well is now flowing at 2,000 barrels

9
00:14:48,210 --> 00:14:51,370
   and it's paying me an income of $5,000 a week.

10
00:14:52,050 --> 00:14:55,350
I have two others drilling and I have 16 producing at Antelope,

11
00:14:55,480 --> 00:14:59,890
so, ladies and gentlemen, if I say I'm an oilman, you will agree.

12
00:15:02,720 --> 00:15:05,390
Now, you have a great chance here,

13
00:15:05,530 --> 00:15:08,390
but bear in mind you could lose it all if you're not careful.

14
00:15:08,530 --> 00:15:10,900
Out of all men that beg for a chance to drill your lots,

15
00:15:11,030 --> 00:15:14,230
maybe one in twenty will be oilmen.

16
00:15:14,340 --> 00:15:15,560
The rest will be speculators,

17
00:15:15,670 --> 00:15:18,200
that's men trying to get between you and the oilmen

18
00:15:18,310 --> 00:15:21,900
to get some of the money that ought, by rights, come to you.

19
00:15:22,010 --> 00:15:24,950
Even if you find one that has money and means to drill,

20
00:15:25,080 --> 00:15:27,510
he'll maybe know nothing about drilling.

21
00:15:27,620 --> 00:15:29,580
He'll have to hire the job out on contract,

22
00:15:29,720 --> 00:15:32,520
and then you're depending on a contractor,

23
00:15:32,620 --> 00:15:33,680
who'll rush the job through

24
00:15:33,790 --> 00:15:35,880
so he can get another contract just as quick as he can.

25
00:15:35,990 --> 00:15:37,550
This is the way that this works.

26
00:15:37,660 --> 00:15:40,920
What is your offer? We're wasting time.

27
00:15:41,230 --> 00:15:42,200
Please!

28
00:15:45,430 --> 00:15:47,370
I do my own drilling.

29
00:15:48,040 --> 00:15:51,900
And the men that work for me, work for me, and they are men I know.

30
00:15:52,040 --> 00:15:55,740
I make it my business to be there and to see their work.

31
00:15:55,880 --> 00:15:58,940
I don't lose my tools in the hole and spend months fishing for them.

32
00:15:59,080 --> 00:16:00,210
I don't botch the cementing off

33
00:16:00,320 --> 00:16:03,880
and let water in the hole and ruin the whole lease.

34
00:16:04,020 --> 00:16:06,010
I'm a family man.

35
00:16:06,120 --> 00:16:10,750
I run a family business. This is my son and my partner, H.W. Plainview.

36
00:16:11,760 --> 00:16:16,560
We offer you the bond of family that very few oilmen can understand.

37
00:16:18,530 --> 00:16:21,590
I'm fixed like no other company in this field

38
00:16:21,740 --> 00:16:24,900
and that's because my Coyote Hills well has just come in.

39
00:16:25,040 --> 00:16:27,470
I have a string of tools all ready to put to work.

40
00:16:27,580 --> 00:16:29,700
I can load a rig onto trucks and have them here in a week.

41
00:16:29,840 --> 00:16:32,900
I have business connections, so I can get the lumber for the derricks.

42
00:16:33,050 --> 00:16:36,810
Such things go by friendship in a rush like this.

43
00:16:36,950 --> 00:16:40,790
And this is why I can guarantee to start drilling

44
00:16:40,920 --> 00:16:43,860
and to put up the cash to back my word.

45
00:16:43,960 --> 00:16:45,520
I assure you, ladies and gentlemen,

46
00:16:45,630 --> 00:16:48,930
no matter what the others promise to do,

47
00:16:49,060 --> 00:16:52,460
when it comes to the showdown, they won't be there.

48
00:16:53,740 --> 00:16:56,700
Sit down! Sit down, you have no right...

49
00:16:57,570 --> 00:16:59,730
Let us discuss what the man has to say.

50
00:16:59,840 --> 00:17:02,830
Let us discuss what the man has to say.

51
00:16:59,910 --> 00:17:02,900
- Prescott, do you trust this man? - Let's discuss what he has to say.

52
00:17:02,940 --> 00:17:06,400
- There's logic to what he's saying. - How does he know? My lot is there!

53
00:17:08,250 --> 00:17:11,380
Two or three years, it could be ten years!

54
00:17:11,490 --> 00:17:14,610
- We gain nothing by losing our heads! - Look at that well out there!

55
00:17:14,720 --> 00:17:16,250
Nobody's losing their heads.

56
00:17:17,230 --> 00:17:19,790
You have no business being here!

57
00:17:20,760 --> 00:17:23,230
Sit that woman down, sir!

58
00:17:24,900 --> 00:17:26,260
You can sit down.

59
00:17:26,400 --> 00:17:28,870
Mr. Plainview! Please, Mr. Plainview.

60
00:17:29,970 --> 00:17:31,960
No, Mr. Plainview! No, where are you going?

61
00:17:32,070 --> 00:17:35,170
- I don't need the lease. Thank you. - But we need you.

62
00:17:35,280 --> 00:17:37,510
Too much confusion. Thank you for your time.

63
00:17:37,610 --> 00:17:39,270
No, no, there's no confusion.

64
00:17:39,410 --> 00:17:43,080
I wouldn't take the lease if you gave it to me as a gift.

65
00:17:53,760 --> 00:17:56,530
   Mr. Bankside, I'm not going to waste your time.

66
00:17:56,630 --> 00:17:59,100
   I'd certainly appreciate it if you didn't waste mine.

67
00:17:59,200 --> 00:18:03,930
Now, if you wish to sign with me, we can have a well drilling within 10 days.

68
00:18:04,040 --> 00:18:07,440
Your lot is further north from the discovery well up here.

69
00:18:07,610 --> 00:18:10,130
That means we'll probably have to dig deeper.

70
00:18:10,280 --> 00:18:12,640
And if there's as much oil here as I think there is,

71
00:18:12,780 --> 00:18:15,770
it'll be harder to reach, but once we find it, we can take it right out.

72
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:20,480
We have to act quickly, because very soon these fields will be dry.

73
00:18:20,620 --> 00:18:22,920
I need you to know what you want to do.

74
00:18:23,020 --> 00:18:26,050
Now, because of the distance from the discovery well,

75
00:18:26,160 --> 00:18:28,420
I'll pay you a smaller royalty than you'd get down there

76
00:18:28,530 --> 00:18:32,360
but I'm prepared to give you a $1,000 bonus on your lot.

77
00:18:32,470 --> 00:18:34,030
What kind of royalty are you talking about?

78
00:18:34,140 --> 00:18:38,570
One-sixth, plus a guarantee to start drilling within 10 days.

79
00:18:38,670 --> 00:18:41,900
Now, that's something you won't find anywhere else.

80
00:18:50,820 --> 00:18:52,790
What age are your children, ma'am?

81
00:18:52,920 --> 00:18:54,620
Ten and twelve.

82
00:18:55,760 --> 00:18:59,620
Mr. Plainview, a question, sir. Where is your wife?

83
00:19:01,760 --> 00:19:04,600
She died in childbirth, Mrs. Bankside.

84
00:19:05,700 --> 00:19:08,000
So it's just me and my son now.

85
00:19:14,880 --> 00:19:16,740
It's coming in, boss!

86
00:19:17,180 --> 00:19:18,480
Hear it?

87
00:19:44,770 --> 00:19:46,470
Mr. Plainview?

88
00:19:46,570 --> 00:19:47,800
Yes?

89
00:19:50,040 --> 00:19:52,140
Are you Daniel Plainview?

90
00:19:54,050 --> 00:19:55,170
Yes.

91
00:19:56,850 --> 00:19:58,820
What can I do for you?

92
00:20:00,660 --> 00:20:02,450
You look for oil.

93
00:20:03,690 --> 00:20:05,160
That's right.

94
00:20:05,290 --> 00:20:08,320
What do you pay for a place that has it?

95
00:20:08,460 --> 00:20:11,450
- Well, that depends. - What does it depend on?

96
00:20:13,500 --> 00:20:15,330
On a lot of things.

97
00:20:16,270 --> 00:20:21,260
If I told you I knew a place that had oil where land could be bought cheaply,

98
00:20:21,380 --> 00:20:24,140
what do you think that would be worth?

99
00:20:25,150 --> 00:20:29,380
I think that you should let me know what you know

100
00:20:29,480 --> 00:20:32,610
and then we'll try and work something out.

101
00:20:34,660 --> 00:20:36,780
- Can I sit down? - Please.

102
00:20:47,940 --> 00:20:50,230
What church do you belong to?

103
00:20:55,940 --> 00:20:57,240
I...

104
00:20:59,410 --> 00:21:02,910
I enjoy all faiths. I don't belong to one church in particular.

105
00:21:03,050 --> 00:21:07,040
I like them all. I like everything. Where are you from?

106
00:21:07,150 --> 00:21:11,020
That would be telling you. That's what I want to sell you.

107
00:21:13,590 --> 00:21:16,150
What are you doing in Signal Hill?

108
00:21:16,260 --> 00:21:18,660
We have oil, and it seeps through the ground.

109
00:21:18,770 --> 00:21:20,320
Do you want to pay me to know where it is?

110
00:21:20,430 --> 00:21:21,490
Just 'cause there's something on the ground

111
00:21:21,600 --> 00:21:23,370
doesn't mean there's anything beneath it.

112
00:21:23,470 --> 00:21:26,200
Why did Standard Oil buy up land?

113
00:21:28,780 --> 00:21:30,640
Is it in California?

114
00:21:31,580 --> 00:21:34,710
- Maybe. - How much land did they buy?

115
00:21:34,850 --> 00:21:38,250
I'd like it better if you didn't think I was stupid.

116
00:21:46,690 --> 00:21:49,030
Why did you come to me?

117
00:21:49,160 --> 00:21:53,460
- You just brought this well in. - That's right.

118
00:21:53,570 --> 00:21:57,870
Yes, so just give me $500 in cash right now

119
00:21:58,010 --> 00:22:00,440
and I'll tell you where it is.

120
00:22:00,540 --> 00:22:02,810
I'll tell you what I'll do, son. I'll give you $100 now,

121
00:22:02,910 --> 00:22:07,540
and if it proves to be a promising lease, then give you a $1,000 bonus.

122
00:22:07,680 --> 00:22:09,620
Six hundred dollars.

123
00:22:12,450 --> 00:22:15,320
Tell me one thing to help me decide. What else have you got up there?

124
00:22:15,420 --> 00:22:17,120
What do you grow?

125
00:22:17,220 --> 00:22:20,960
We have a big ranch, but it's mostly rocks.

126
00:22:21,060 --> 00:22:23,530
Plant things. Nothing will grow but weeds.

127
00:22:23,660 --> 00:22:24,860
What makes you think it's up?

128
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:28,060
Is there sulfur around? Or alkali deposits?

129
00:22:28,200 --> 00:22:31,230
Alkali nearby. I don't know sulfur.

130
00:22:37,810 --> 00:22:39,610
Is that your son?

131
00:22:40,050 --> 00:22:41,340
Yes.

132
00:22:42,680 --> 00:22:43,950
- Hi. - Hi.

133
00:22:47,150 --> 00:22:49,990
- Who are you? - I'm Fletcher Hamilton.

134
00:22:50,120 --> 00:22:52,090
Nice to meet you, son. What's your name?

135
00:22:52,190 --> 00:22:53,820
What do you do?

136
00:22:54,830 --> 00:22:56,920
I work with Mr. Plainview.

137
00:22:57,630 --> 00:22:59,360
Here's $500, son.

138
00:22:59,500 --> 00:23:03,330
You tell me something worth hearing, this money's yours.

139
00:23:07,310 --> 00:23:11,180
I come from a town called Little Boston in Isabella County.

140
00:23:13,350 --> 00:23:17,780
This is us, here. Spur station here at Little Boston.

141
00:23:17,890 --> 00:23:20,880
The Sunday ranch is what you're looking for.

142
00:23:20,990 --> 00:23:23,220
There's a sheep trail that takes you there.

143
00:23:23,320 --> 00:23:26,290
It's a mile out of town headed west, not far.

144
00:23:26,430 --> 00:23:30,330
Just through a small pass here near the base of the hills.

145
00:23:30,460 --> 00:23:34,160
You'll pass a church and just follow the sheep trail.

146
00:23:34,300 --> 00:23:38,430
- Where's Standard buying up? - Here and here.

147
00:23:40,610 --> 00:23:43,040
- Your family name is Sunday, yes? - That's right.

148
00:23:43,140 --> 00:23:44,610
How many's in your family?

149
00:23:44,750 --> 00:23:47,940
My father and mother and sisters and my brother Eli.

150
00:23:48,080 --> 00:23:50,740
- How many sisters do you have? - Two.

151
00:23:50,850 --> 00:23:53,180
- What's your name? - Paul.

152
00:23:53,290 --> 00:23:56,520
Does any of your family know about the oil that you say is there?

153
00:23:56,620 --> 00:23:58,060
I don't know.

154
00:23:58,160 --> 00:24:00,750
My uncle always said there was oil there,

155
00:24:00,900 --> 00:24:03,360
but I don't know what they heard or what they think.

156
00:24:03,460 --> 00:24:04,900
What do you grow?

157
00:24:05,000 --> 00:24:10,160
lt's goats. It's a goat farm. I told you, nothing grows but weeds.

158
00:24:10,270 --> 00:24:12,760
- Is there water? - It's salty.

159
00:24:12,910 --> 00:24:16,270
You drill a well, it's hard not to get saltwater.

160
00:24:18,150 --> 00:24:21,550
The oil is there. I'm telling you.

161
00:24:26,190 --> 00:24:29,380
- I want to go now, so... - You can stay tonight.

162
00:24:29,520 --> 00:24:33,580
- No, I want to go now. I want to leave. - Listen, Paul.

163
00:24:35,460 --> 00:24:40,230
If I travel all the way out there and I find that you've been lying to me,

164
00:24:40,370 --> 00:24:42,960
I'm going to find you and I'm going to take more than my money back.

165
00:24:43,070 --> 00:24:45,300
Is that all right with you?

166
00:24:45,410 --> 00:24:47,640
- Yes, sir. - All right, then.

167
00:24:48,380 --> 00:24:52,510
- Nice luck to you. God bless. - And to you, young man.

168
00:26:31,950 --> 00:26:33,940
- There's someone coming. - Thank you, Mary.

169
00:26:43,690 --> 00:26:47,220
- Good evening. - Good evening.

170
00:26:49,760 --> 00:26:53,030
My name's Daniel Plainview. This is my son, H.W.

171
00:26:53,900 --> 00:26:56,670
- Are you hunting? - Hunting for quail.

172
00:26:56,770 --> 00:26:59,640
We're told there might be a good place to camp up near the Sunday ranch.

173
00:26:59,740 --> 00:27:01,570
This is the Sunday ranch. You can camp here.

174
00:27:01,710 --> 00:27:04,410
- Thank you. Do you have water? - Yes.

175
00:27:05,410 --> 00:27:07,400
We heard there was an earthquake up here a few days ago.

176
00:27:07,550 --> 00:27:09,380
- Is that right? - Yes.

177
00:27:10,250 --> 00:27:13,910
- Your family? - Yeah, all fine. Thank you.

178
00:27:15,560 --> 00:27:18,990
- We have goat's milk, if you'd like. - That would be fine.

179
00:27:21,030 --> 00:27:22,000
Now,

180
00:27:23,900 --> 00:27:27,960
if we set our tent away over there, we'd be out of your way over there.

181
00:27:28,070 --> 00:27:29,330
That's fine.

182
00:27:29,440 --> 00:27:31,630
Ruth! Help these men and bring them some water.

183
00:27:31,740 --> 00:27:33,170
No! H.W.

184
00:27:35,080 --> 00:27:38,530
Mr. Plainview, would you like that milk now?

185
00:27:38,680 --> 00:27:42,740
- That would be fine. Thank you. - Mary! Bring them some milk.

186
00:27:42,880 --> 00:27:44,320
My family will help you set up your tent.

187
00:27:44,420 --> 00:27:46,650
No, please. We set ourselves on this camping trip.

188
00:27:46,750 --> 00:27:48,420
We have to do the camping.

189
00:27:48,560 --> 00:27:49,920
Hurry up!

190
00:27:52,890 --> 00:27:56,890
- Do you have bread? - We have potatoes.

191
00:27:57,030 --> 00:27:58,660
Potatoes would be nice, thank you.

192
00:27:58,770 --> 00:28:00,230
I'll have them boil you up some potatoes.

193
00:28:00,370 --> 00:28:02,670
That's all right. I thought maybe we'd make a fire.

194
00:28:02,770 --> 00:28:05,000
I wanted to work with my son on making a fire.

195
00:28:05,110 --> 00:28:07,040
All right. My son, Eli, will bring you some wood.

196
00:28:07,170 --> 00:28:09,200
Thank you so much for your hospitality, Mr. Sunday.

197
00:28:09,340 --> 00:28:11,370
- Yes. - And we'll be out of your way.

198
00:28:11,480 --> 00:28:14,210
- We're just hunting for quail. - Yes.

199
00:28:16,180 --> 00:28:18,340
- I'm sorry we don't have any bread. - No, no, no.

200
00:28:18,450 --> 00:28:21,250
Corn doesn't fill out in the hills here. It's mostly rock.

201
00:28:21,390 --> 00:28:24,190
We don't have room to raise the grain.

202
00:28:27,930 --> 00:28:29,990
Thank you, young lady.

203
00:28:55,220 --> 00:28:56,850
My name is Eli.

204
00:28:58,190 --> 00:29:00,160
Yes, you're Eli Sunday.

205
00:29:01,160 --> 00:29:02,560
Welcome.

206
00:29:06,270 --> 00:29:07,960
- H.W. - Eli.

207
00:29:13,270 --> 00:29:16,370
- You're hunting quail? - That's right.

208
00:29:20,650 --> 00:29:25,140
- We will bring dinner. - Thank you. Thank you so much.

209
00:30:47,230 --> 00:30:48,430
Dad!

210
00:30:49,140 --> 00:30:50,870
Dad, look at my shoe.

211
00:31:17,360 --> 00:31:19,990
That's earthquake oil. Set loose.

212
00:31:43,520 --> 00:31:44,820
   So...

213
00:31:46,430 --> 00:31:47,620
   So?

214
00:31:48,500 --> 00:31:49,860
   So, so.

215
00:31:50,660 --> 00:31:53,960
   If there's anything here, we take it to the sea.

216
00:31:55,100 --> 00:31:58,830
What we do is we build a pipeline to Port Hueneme or Santa Paula,

217
00:31:58,940 --> 00:32:00,460
it's about 100 miles,

218
00:32:00,570 --> 00:32:04,480
and we do a deal with Union Oil. This is what we do.

219
00:32:05,010 --> 00:32:07,980
Then we don't need the railroads and their shipping costs anymore.

220
00:32:08,080 --> 00:32:09,480
You see?

221
00:32:12,320 --> 00:32:13,340
Yeah.

222
00:32:13,490 --> 00:32:16,090
- You see that? - Yeah.

223
00:32:17,220 --> 00:32:19,450
Then we're making money. We're making the real money.

224
00:32:19,560 --> 00:32:21,390
What we should be making. Not just...

225
00:32:21,530 --> 00:32:23,890
Not just throwing it away on shipping costs.

226
00:32:24,030 --> 00:32:26,160
Otherwise, it's just mud.

227
00:32:30,400 --> 00:32:32,960
How much are we going to pay them?

228
00:32:33,840 --> 00:32:35,330
Who's that?

229
00:32:38,050 --> 00:32:39,840
The Sunday family.

230
00:32:40,410 --> 00:32:43,280
I'm not going to give them oil prices.

231
00:32:45,850 --> 00:32:48,120
I'll give them quail prices.

232
00:32:53,860 --> 00:32:55,490
If we could take a few minutes,

233
00:32:55,600 --> 00:32:58,720
there's something I'd very much like to talk with you about.

234
00:32:58,870 --> 00:33:02,200
Mother, would you take the girls outside, please?

235
00:33:14,410 --> 00:33:17,180
I believe in plain speaking, so...

236
00:33:17,320 --> 00:33:20,980
This is a beautiful ranch. I love hunting for quail.

237
00:33:21,860 --> 00:33:24,920
My boy has been sick, you know. He needs fresh air.

238
00:33:25,030 --> 00:33:28,260
Doctors all say he needs plentiful fresh air.

239
00:33:30,100 --> 00:33:31,060
So,

240
00:33:33,670 --> 00:33:37,630
what would you say would be a fair price for this lot, Abel?

241
00:33:38,770 --> 00:33:41,330
- To buy this place? - That's right.

242
00:33:46,350 --> 00:33:48,140
Take a moment.

243
00:33:52,020 --> 00:33:55,750
- I'm sorry. I don't know. - Six dollars an acre.

244
00:33:55,860 --> 00:33:59,290
Six dollars? Thank you, Eli.

245
00:33:59,430 --> 00:34:03,120
And then with the improvements to the ranch over the years at $500...

246
00:34:03,260 --> 00:34:05,790
I'd like to offer you $3,700 for this ranch.

247
00:34:05,930 --> 00:34:08,490
- That's $3,700. - No.

248
00:34:09,440 --> 00:34:11,730
The Lord has sent this man here, Eli.

249
00:34:11,840 --> 00:34:13,330
Yes, I believe He has.

250
00:34:13,470 --> 00:34:17,530
- My offer to you is $3,700. - What is it that brought you here, sir?

251
00:34:18,750 --> 00:34:20,410
The Good Lord's guidance.

252
00:34:20,510 --> 00:34:21,850
- Now, of course, within that... - What about our oil?

253
00:34:21,950 --> 00:34:23,610
...we're going to develop a lease.

254
00:34:24,920 --> 00:34:28,410
- What's that? - What about our oil?

255
00:34:29,820 --> 00:34:31,260
What about it?

256
00:34:31,360 --> 00:34:33,550
We have oil here. That's worth something.

257
00:34:33,660 --> 00:34:36,090
Do you have someone who can drill for it?

258
00:34:36,200 --> 00:34:38,130
- Do you think there's oil here? - I know there is.

259
00:34:38,270 --> 00:34:40,290
It's very expensive to drill.

260
00:34:40,430 --> 00:34:42,600
To get it up and out of the ground. You ever tried that before?

261
00:34:42,700 --> 00:34:44,760
- How much is it? - Costly.

262
00:34:44,870 --> 00:34:47,930
Well, our oil sits right up on top of the ground.

263
00:34:48,980 --> 00:34:50,700
I believe that's called seepage.

264
00:34:50,840 --> 00:34:52,330
Doesn't necessarily mean there's anything underneath.

265
00:34:52,480 --> 00:34:54,640
- What would you give us for it? - I don't know.

266
00:34:54,750 --> 00:34:57,680
- Something you don't know. - That's right.

267
00:35:00,990 --> 00:35:02,960
What would you like, Eli?

268
00:35:04,690 --> 00:35:06,990
Ten thousand dollars.

269
00:35:09,200 --> 00:35:10,660
For what?

270
00:35:12,630 --> 00:35:14,330
For my church.

271
00:35:24,280 --> 00:35:25,770
That's good.

272
00:35:28,780 --> 00:35:30,580
That's a good one.

273
00:35:32,250 --> 00:35:33,220
Well...

274
00:35:34,490 --> 00:35:38,080
If we decide to drill for oil and if the well begins to produce,

275
00:35:38,190 --> 00:35:39,890
I'll give your church a $5,000 signing bonus.

276
00:35:39,990 --> 00:35:40,960
Ten thousand.

277
00:35:41,060 --> 00:35:43,550
Do you want to find someone else that's going to come here and drill, Eli?

278
00:35:43,660 --> 00:35:46,760
Make the investment and do all the hard work that goes into it?

279
00:35:46,900 --> 00:35:50,770
I can just as easily hunt for quail on another ranch as I can here, so...

280
00:35:50,900 --> 00:35:55,530
Though I'll happily be a supporter of your church for as long as I can.

281
00:35:55,640 --> 00:35:57,440
For the bonus only.

282
00:35:59,250 --> 00:36:03,050
Now, as it happens, I do have some connections in the drilling business

283
00:36:03,150 --> 00:36:07,710
who might help get us started. How do you feel about this, Abel?

284
00:36:07,820 --> 00:36:09,720
Yes. What Eli says.

285
00:36:09,860 --> 00:36:13,020
Well, good! Let's draw up some contracts and let's...

286
00:36:13,130 --> 00:36:15,030
Let's give it a try.

287
00:36:16,400 --> 00:36:19,230
Appreciate your help with this, Eli.

288
00:36:30,540 --> 00:36:32,170
- Good afternoon. - Good afternoon.

289
00:36:32,280 --> 00:36:33,580
- Real estate? - Yes.

290
00:36:33,710 --> 00:36:35,700
Yes, I'd like to talk to you.

291
00:36:35,850 --> 00:36:40,340
I'm looking for some land. I just bought the Sunday ranch.

292
00:36:40,490 --> 00:36:44,510
And, well, where's the map?

293
00:36:45,090 --> 00:36:47,530
Where are the hills behind the Sunday ranch?

294
00:36:47,660 --> 00:36:51,320
That's here. It's the Bandy tract. He has over 600 acres.

295
00:36:51,430 --> 00:36:55,490
Bandy, 600.

296
00:36:55,640 --> 00:37:02,100
- What about this? - A.C. Maude, Blodget, Redlick, Carr.

297
00:37:03,810 --> 00:37:06,800
- What's it held at? - Six dollars an acre.

298
00:37:07,550 --> 00:37:08,840
Six.

299
00:37:08,980 --> 00:37:10,610
What about this?

300
00:37:10,720 --> 00:37:14,310
That's the Belvins, and that could be got, I'm sure.

301
00:37:16,220 --> 00:37:18,920
Can everything around here be got?

302
00:37:19,690 --> 00:37:21,160
Sure.

303
00:37:45,490 --> 00:37:48,940
Paul Sunday turned out to be a good friend of ours.

304
00:37:49,660 --> 00:37:51,250
That's right.

305
00:37:53,590 --> 00:37:57,590
Well, you get here just as soon as you can. Bring Fred English.

306
00:37:58,970 --> 00:38:00,400
Good enough.

307
00:38:01,070 --> 00:38:02,800
Thank you, porter.

308
00:38:05,410 --> 00:38:08,030
- H.W., how are you? - Fine, and you?

309
00:38:08,140 --> 00:38:10,040
- Pretty good. Where's your dad? - He's inside.

310
00:38:10,140 --> 00:38:11,540
You fellas are a long way from Signal Hill.

311
00:38:11,650 --> 00:38:13,610
- Hello, Plainview. - Hello, Gene.

312
00:38:13,750 --> 00:38:16,240
- Good to see you. - Charlie.

313
00:38:16,380 --> 00:38:20,910
- On your way somewhere else? - Passing through. Looking around.

314
00:38:21,050 --> 00:38:23,550
- Funny to see you. - Funny, isn't it?

315
00:38:23,690 --> 00:38:26,420
You boys are a regular family business.

316
00:38:26,560 --> 00:38:28,220
You boys are a little late.

317
00:38:28,360 --> 00:38:32,390
- What did you find? - I found some interesting prospects.

318
00:38:32,530 --> 00:38:33,760
Did you hear Standard bought up?

319
00:38:33,900 --> 00:38:36,490
- Mostly in the north, so far. - That's what I hear.

320
00:38:36,600 --> 00:38:40,040
I'm gonna tell you, Gene, if you're gonna make a play, look east.

321
00:38:40,170 --> 00:38:45,410
I'd rather it be you than someone else. This mud around here has been taken.

322
00:38:45,550 --> 00:38:49,070
It must be easy when you have such a cute face to carry around with you.

323
00:38:49,220 --> 00:38:52,280
- Telling me how handsome my son is? - Well, that I am.

324
00:38:52,390 --> 00:38:55,550
That's very nice. Thank you. Good luck, Gene.

325
00:38:55,690 --> 00:38:58,160
- Take care. - Like I said, go east.

326
00:38:58,260 --> 00:38:59,350
H.W.

327
00:39:00,390 --> 00:39:03,060
I'll be your lawyer if you need to draw up a contract.

328
00:39:03,200 --> 00:39:07,460
Make sure you don't get swindled, boy. Get half what your dad's making.

329
00:39:17,740 --> 00:39:19,340
How's that?

330
00:39:34,290 --> 00:39:36,460
What are those men doing?

331
00:39:38,800 --> 00:39:41,320
They're just guys that are working for us.

332
00:39:41,470 --> 00:39:43,770
They're just looking around.

333
00:39:45,970 --> 00:39:48,200
How much money can we make?

334
00:39:52,250 --> 00:39:54,610
I don't know. It depends.

335
00:39:58,820 --> 00:40:00,910
One thousand dollars?

336
00:40:08,760 --> 00:40:12,530
Mary said that her father beats her if she doesn't pray.

337
00:40:19,110 --> 00:40:21,540
Mary, she's the smaller one?

338
00:40:24,210 --> 00:40:25,730
Yes, she is.

339
00:40:39,530 --> 00:40:42,050
- Everyone here? - Very successful.

340
00:40:42,830 --> 00:40:43,850
But?

341
00:40:44,000 --> 00:40:47,360
There were a few vacant lots and one holdout.

342
00:40:47,500 --> 00:40:49,130
- Who? - William Bandy.

343
00:40:49,240 --> 00:40:51,290
...eight. Who's he?

344
00:40:51,400 --> 00:40:52,800
He's an old man who homesteaded here.

345
00:40:52,910 --> 00:40:56,030
Lives with his grandson. He said he'd like to speak with you.

346
00:40:56,180 --> 00:40:57,340
Is he here?

347
00:40:57,480 --> 00:41:00,500
No, he'd like you to come visit with him.

348
00:41:00,650 --> 00:41:02,340
He's boosting his price.

349
00:41:02,480 --> 00:41:06,280
He said he'd like to speak with whoever is doing the buying.

350
00:41:06,390 --> 00:41:09,650
Well, let him wait. He'll come around. Let's go.

351
00:41:16,730 --> 00:41:18,660
Ladies and gentlemen?

352
00:41:19,670 --> 00:41:21,690
Ladies and gentlemen.

353
00:41:21,840 --> 00:41:25,200
Thank you so much for visiting with us this evening.

354
00:41:25,340 --> 00:41:28,900
Now, I've traveled across half our state to be here and to see about this land.

355
00:41:31,980 --> 00:41:33,470
   Now, I daresay some of you might have heard

356
00:41:33,610 --> 00:41:37,450
   some of the more extravagant rumors about what my plans are,

357
00:41:37,550 --> 00:41:40,310
   so I just thought you'd like to hear it from me.

358
00:41:40,450 --> 00:41:43,320
   This is the face. It's no great mystery.

359
00:41:46,190 --> 00:41:50,150
   I'm an oilman, ladies and gentlemen,

360
00:41:51,030 --> 00:41:54,430
   I have numerous concerns spread across this state.

361
00:41:54,530 --> 00:41:57,940
   I have many wells flowing at many thousand barrels per day,

362
00:41:58,040 --> 00:42:01,010
   so I like to think of myself as an oilman.

363
00:42:02,010 --> 00:42:03,810
   As an oilman, I hope that you'll forgive

364
00:42:03,910 --> 00:42:06,810
   just good old-fashioned plain speaking.

365
00:42:08,450 --> 00:42:11,980
   Now, this work that we do is very much a family enterprise.

366
00:42:12,120 --> 00:42:14,780
   I work side by side with my wonderful son, H. W.

367
00:42:14,890 --> 00:42:18,120
   I think one or two of you might have met him already.

368
00:42:18,220 --> 00:42:21,990
   And I encourage my men to bring their families, as well.

369
00:42:22,130 --> 00:42:26,090
   Of course, it makes for an ever so much more rewarding life for them.

370
00:42:26,200 --> 00:42:30,160
   Family means children, and children means education.

371
00:42:30,300 --> 00:42:33,970
   So, wherever we set up camp, education is a necessity,

372
00:42:34,110 --> 00:42:36,300
   and we're just so happy to take care of that.

373
00:42:36,440 --> 00:42:38,810
So let's build a wonderful school in Little Boston.

374
00:42:38,950 --> 00:42:41,140
These children are the future that we strive for,

375
00:42:41,280 --> 00:42:44,380
and so they should have the very best of things.

376
00:42:44,480 --> 00:42:46,480
Now, something else,

377
00:42:46,620 --> 00:42:50,450
and please don't be insulted if I speak about this. Bread.

378
00:42:50,590 --> 00:42:52,560
Let's talk about bread.

379
00:42:53,260 --> 00:42:56,590
Now, to my mind, it's an abomination to consider

380
00:42:56,730 --> 00:43:00,930
that any man, woman, or child in this magnificent country of ours

381
00:43:01,070 --> 00:43:04,530
should have to look upon a loaf of bread as a luxury.

382
00:43:05,340 --> 00:43:08,900
   We're going to dig water wells here, and water wells means irrigation.

383
00:43:09,040 --> 00:43:11,410
   Irrigation means cultivation.

384
00:43:11,540 --> 00:43:15,410
   We're going to raise crops here where before it just simply wasn't possible.

385
00:43:15,550 --> 00:43:17,950
   You're going to have more grain than you'll know what to do with,

386
00:43:18,080 --> 00:43:21,020
   and bread will be coming right out of your ears, ma'am.

387
00:43:21,120 --> 00:43:26,420
   New roads, agriculture, employment, education.

388
00:43:26,560 --> 00:43:28,530
These are just a few of the things we can offer you,

389
00:43:28,630 --> 00:43:30,600
and I assure you, ladies and gentlemen,

390
00:43:30,730 --> 00:43:32,890
that if we do find oil here,

391
00:43:33,030 --> 00:43:36,430
and I think there's a very good chance that we will,

392
00:43:36,570 --> 00:43:41,060
this community of yours will not only survive, it will flourish.

393
00:43:43,310 --> 00:43:46,340
I'd be happy to answer any questions that you might have. Yes?

394
00:43:46,450 --> 00:43:48,970
Will the new road lead to the church?

395
00:43:49,080 --> 00:43:53,520
That'll be the first place that it leads. Thank you, Eli. Anyone else?

396
00:43:54,190 --> 00:43:56,490
Well, if anything comes up, I'm pretty easy to find.

397
00:43:56,590 --> 00:43:57,850
You just come visit with me.

398
00:43:57,960 --> 00:43:59,980
Thank you so much for your time, and good night.

399
00:44:38,530 --> 00:44:43,490
   What a privilege to carry

400
00:44:43,640 --> 00:44:47,500
   everything to God in prayer!

401
00:44:48,470 --> 00:44:52,040
   What a privilege to carry...

402
00:45:09,400 --> 00:45:11,260
Just follow the new road right to the church.

403
00:45:11,360 --> 00:45:13,590
The new road will lead you there.

404
00:45:13,700 --> 00:45:15,360
Hello, brother, my name is Eli.

405
00:45:15,500 --> 00:45:19,030
The Church of the Third Revelation welcomes you.

406
00:45:19,170 --> 00:45:20,870
Hello, brother, my name is Eli.

407
00:45:21,010 --> 00:45:23,310
The Church of the Third Revelation welcomes you.

408
00:45:23,440 --> 00:45:26,470
Just follow the new road right to the church.

409
00:45:35,320 --> 00:45:38,880
   Jesus knows our every weakness

410
00:45:40,730 --> 00:45:43,660
   Take it to the Lord in prayer

411
00:45:44,900 --> 00:45:49,060
   Are we weak and heavy-laden

412
00:45:50,100 --> 00:45:53,100
   Cumbered with a load of care?

413
00:45:54,340 --> 00:45:57,430
   Precious Savior still our refuge

414
00:45:59,480 --> 00:46:02,070
   Take it to the Lord in prayer...

415
00:46:14,090 --> 00:46:17,150
- Daniel, may I speak with you? - Yes, come in.

416
00:46:19,300 --> 00:46:22,270
I'll bring them up when they arrive.

417
00:46:22,400 --> 00:46:24,600
- Good morning. - Good morning.

418
00:46:24,740 --> 00:46:26,640
How is all the work coming?

419
00:46:26,770 --> 00:46:28,210
Everything's good.

420
00:46:28,310 --> 00:46:31,440
- All the men are provided for? - Of course.

421
00:46:33,510 --> 00:46:35,380
Spirits seem high.

422
00:46:37,850 --> 00:46:41,290
Is there anything that you need from me?

423
00:46:44,390 --> 00:46:48,620
- Anything the church can do for you? - I don't believe so. No. Thank you.

424
00:46:48,760 --> 00:46:51,090
I understand you've asked the people to gather around

425
00:46:51,230 --> 00:46:52,820
and watch the well begin tomorrow. Is that right?

426
00:46:52,930 --> 00:46:54,900
- That's right. - I will bless the well.

427
00:46:56,670 --> 00:46:59,370
Before you begin, you should introduce me.

428
00:46:59,470 --> 00:47:02,030
You'll see me walk up towards the oil well, and when I...

429
00:47:02,140 --> 00:47:03,200
The derrick.

430
00:47:03,310 --> 00:47:07,110
You'll see me walk up, and then you could say my name.

431
00:47:07,250 --> 00:47:09,370
When you walk up?

432
00:47:09,480 --> 00:47:13,380
Yes. You'll see me walk up, and then you could say,

433
00:47:13,490 --> 00:47:18,620
"The proud son of these hills who tended his Father's flock,"

434
00:47:18,860 --> 00:47:21,260
and then you could say my name.

435
00:47:22,560 --> 00:47:24,120
That's fine.

436
00:47:25,130 --> 00:47:28,530
- And what happens then? - Well, then we start the drill.

437
00:47:31,700 --> 00:47:35,330
It's a simple blessing, Daniel, but an important one.

438
00:47:35,470 --> 00:47:38,440
It's just a few words. It won't take long.

439
00:47:39,550 --> 00:47:42,640
- What time? - What time's good for you, Eli?

440
00:47:42,780 --> 00:47:45,580
- 4:00. - Well, let's make it 4:00 then.

441
00:47:46,690 --> 00:47:50,420
- My thanks for your visit. - Good day. Thank you.

442
00:48:05,840 --> 00:48:07,810
Afternoon, everyone.

443
00:48:09,140 --> 00:48:10,730
Come with me.

444
00:48:16,150 --> 00:48:19,610
I thank you all so much for visiting with us at this time.

445
00:48:19,750 --> 00:48:21,550
I've had the pleasure of meeting some of you

446
00:48:21,650 --> 00:48:23,490
and I hope very much in the months to come,

447
00:48:23,620 --> 00:48:26,790
I'll be able to visit with each and every one of you.

448
00:48:26,930 --> 00:48:29,590
I'm better at digging holes in the ground than making speeches,

449
00:48:29,730 --> 00:48:31,250
so let's forget the speech for this evening,

450
00:48:31,400 --> 00:48:33,300
just make it a simple blessing.

451
00:48:33,430 --> 00:48:35,200
You see, one man doesn't prospect from the ground.

452
00:48:35,300 --> 00:48:39,240
It takes a whole community of good people, such as yourselves,

453
00:48:39,340 --> 00:48:42,330
and this is good. We stay together.

454
00:48:42,440 --> 00:48:44,200
We pray together, we work together,

455
00:48:44,310 --> 00:48:47,280
and if the Good Lord smiles kindly on our endeavor,

456
00:48:47,410 --> 00:48:49,880
we share in the wealth together.

457
00:48:52,320 --> 00:48:54,380
Now, before we spud in Mary's Well Number One,

458
00:48:54,490 --> 00:48:57,650
named for the lovely Miss Mary Sunday, here by my side,

459
00:48:57,760 --> 00:49:00,750
a proud daughter of these hills,

460
00:49:00,890 --> 00:49:04,590
I'd just like to say God bless these honest labors of ours, and, of course,

461
00:49:04,730 --> 00:49:06,760
God bless you all.

462
00:49:06,900 --> 00:49:07,990
Amen.

463
00:49:08,100 --> 00:49:09,400
Now go.

464
00:49:14,370 --> 00:49:16,140
Won't be a minute.

465
00:49:19,210 --> 00:49:21,180
Fast as you can, H.W.

466
00:49:24,680 --> 00:49:26,810
Are you ready to do this?

467
00:49:36,660 --> 00:49:39,130
That's it, ladies and gentlemen!

468
00:49:43,040 --> 00:49:47,130
Al Rose has very generously provided some refreshments for this occasion

469
00:49:47,240 --> 00:49:49,970
out of his own pocket. Thank you, Al.

470
00:49:50,710 --> 00:49:55,150
If you'll all just care to help yourselves, I'll be back in a minute.

471
00:51:08,010 --> 00:51:09,530
Mary.

472
00:51:11,210 --> 00:51:12,840
Mary Sunday.

473
00:51:15,680 --> 00:51:18,410
- Do you like your new dress? - Yes. Thank you.

474
00:51:18,520 --> 00:51:21,420
You're welcome. I thought you'd like it.

475
00:51:22,290 --> 00:51:24,810
- Are you happy I came here? - Yes.

476
00:51:26,530 --> 00:51:30,220
Your daddy doesn't hit you anymore, does he? Does he now?

477
00:51:31,100 --> 00:51:32,960
Better not, right?

478
00:51:33,630 --> 00:51:35,620
I'll take care of you.

479
00:51:36,740 --> 00:51:41,870
No more hitting, right? No more hitting. Now go.

480
00:51:42,010 --> 00:51:45,030
Go and play some more and don't come back.

481
00:51:54,190 --> 00:51:55,620
Daniel?

482
00:51:59,290 --> 00:52:03,460
lt's okay, H.W. Go back to sleep. Go on. Go back to sleep.

483
00:52:06,000 --> 00:52:07,160
Daniel.

484
00:52:09,570 --> 00:52:10,760
Daniel.

485
00:52:13,710 --> 00:52:14,970
Daniel!

486
00:52:16,540 --> 00:52:17,740
Daniel!

487
00:52:17,840 --> 00:52:19,110
What?

488
00:52:20,980 --> 00:52:23,070
Lost a man down the well.

489
00:52:27,620 --> 00:52:29,750
- What man? - Joe Gundha.

490
00:52:31,760 --> 00:52:33,820
- Did I know him? - No.

491
00:52:34,330 --> 00:52:35,380
What happened?

492
00:52:43,070 --> 00:52:44,470
Pick it up.

493
00:52:45,140 --> 00:52:46,730
Set the brake.

494
00:52:46,840 --> 00:52:49,140
- Tie it down. - Tie it on.

495
00:52:53,750 --> 00:52:55,080
Shit!

496
00:52:57,150 --> 00:52:59,950
God damn it. Where's the body?

497
00:53:00,290 --> 00:53:03,280
- They're fishing it out now. - All right.

498
00:53:06,660 --> 00:53:09,290
- Where's the bit? - It's on the deck.

499
00:53:52,840 --> 00:53:55,670
Clean him up. Put some clothes on him.

500
00:53:56,810 --> 00:53:58,070
And...

501
00:53:59,710 --> 00:54:01,270
Set up a tent.

502
00:54:01,380 --> 00:54:05,340
Anyone goes down into the cellar, you tell somebody. Yes?

503
00:54:05,980 --> 00:54:07,380
- Yes, sir. - Yes, sir.

504
00:54:11,320 --> 00:54:13,350
Shut down till midday.

505
00:54:44,660 --> 00:54:50,060
And I had a vision. Yes, last night, I had a vision

506
00:54:50,160 --> 00:54:53,060
and I felt God's breath move through me.

507
00:54:56,700 --> 00:55:00,800
And it rolled down into my stomach.

508
00:55:02,810 --> 00:55:04,670
It sloshed around.

509
00:55:06,080 --> 00:55:09,950
And my stomach spoke in a whisper, not a shout,

510
00:55:13,190 --> 00:55:17,380
"Touch this woman with your hands and caress her." Yes.

511
00:55:21,760 --> 00:55:23,920
My dear Mrs. Hunter,

512
00:55:25,100 --> 00:55:27,430
you have arthritis, don't you?

513
00:55:27,570 --> 00:55:29,560
- Yes, I do, Eli. - Yes.

514
00:55:29,670 --> 00:55:33,260
The devil is in your hands, and I will suck it out.

515
00:55:34,440 --> 00:55:38,900
Now, I will not cast this ghost out with a fever

516
00:55:39,040 --> 00:55:44,070
for the new spirit inside me has shown me I have a new way to communicate.

517
00:55:46,550 --> 00:55:48,580
It is a gentle whisper.

518
00:55:54,960 --> 00:55:57,330
Get out of here, ghost.

519
00:55:59,900 --> 00:56:02,230
Get out of here, ghost.

520
00:56:04,270 --> 00:56:05,700
Get out.

521
00:56:06,300 --> 00:56:09,210
Get out of here, ghost.

522
00:56:11,580 --> 00:56:14,740
Get out of here, ghost.

523
00:56:14,880 --> 00:56:18,780
...and enter this woman's body now. - Get out of here, ghost.

524
00:56:18,880 --> 00:56:23,720
Get out of here. Don't you dare turn around and come back.

525
00:56:24,920 --> 00:56:26,620
For if you do,

526
00:56:26,730 --> 00:56:32,220
all the armies of my boot will kick you in the teeth

527
00:56:32,360 --> 00:56:35,860
and you will be cast up and thrown in the dirt

528
00:56:36,000 --> 00:56:38,370
and thrust back to perdition!

529
00:56:38,500 --> 00:56:42,200
And as long as I have teeth, I will bite you,

530
00:56:42,340 --> 00:56:46,300
and if I have no teeth, I will gum you!

531
00:56:46,410 --> 00:56:50,140
And as long as I have fists, I will bash you!

532
00:56:50,250 --> 00:56:54,980
Now, get out of here, ghost! Get out of here, ghost!

533
00:56:55,120 --> 00:56:58,150
Get out of here, ghost!

534
00:57:01,330 --> 00:57:02,920
And it left!

535
00:57:03,700 --> 00:57:05,690
- Hallelujah! - Hallelujah!

536
00:57:07,230 --> 00:57:09,670
- Praise the Lord and his holy days! - Praise God!

537
00:57:09,800 --> 00:57:13,240
- Amen! Thank you. - Thank you, Jesus. Thank you, God.

538
00:57:14,510 --> 00:57:16,670
My dear Mrs. Hunter.

539
00:57:20,280 --> 00:57:22,010
Dance with me.

540
00:57:29,250 --> 00:57:31,590
- Thanks for coming. - It was a wonderful sermon.

541
00:57:31,690 --> 00:57:34,090
- Will I see you tomorrow? - Yes.

542
00:57:39,100 --> 00:57:40,060
Eli.

543
00:57:42,630 --> 00:57:45,430
Had a tragedy at the well last night.

544
00:57:46,670 --> 00:57:48,370
Yes, I heard.

545
00:57:48,470 --> 00:57:50,870
Joe Gundha was a man of considerable faith.

546
00:57:50,980 --> 00:57:55,210
So if you wish to say a few words, his burial is at noon tomorrow.

547
00:57:55,310 --> 00:57:58,150
Daniel, this accident could have been avoided.

548
00:57:58,280 --> 00:58:00,380
It is terrible to think of that well

549
00:58:00,490 --> 00:58:02,350
- working away out there... - These men work in 12-hour shifts.

550
00:58:02,450 --> 00:58:03,440
...unblessed. - They need their rest.

551
00:58:03,590 --> 00:58:05,320
If they don't have it, they start to make stupid mistakes.

552
00:58:05,420 --> 00:58:08,190
I've seen the men drinking. Don't you think that has something to do with this?

553
00:58:08,290 --> 00:58:09,760
We need these men well-rested to bring in this well.

554
00:58:09,890 --> 00:58:12,060
They can't get that if they're up here listening to your gospel,

555
00:58:12,160 --> 00:58:14,290
and then the well can't produce and blow gold all over the place.

556
00:58:14,430 --> 00:58:16,400
I wish I had more time with Joe Gundha.

557
00:58:16,530 --> 00:58:17,730
More could have been done.

558
00:58:17,870 --> 00:58:22,860
Then the well can't produce and blow gold all over the place.

559
00:58:29,210 --> 00:58:31,510
Now, would you see to it that his personal possessions

560
00:58:31,620 --> 00:58:33,740
find their way back to his family, please?

561
00:58:33,890 --> 00:58:35,350
Thank you.

562
00:58:35,890 --> 00:58:39,020
Heard you were planning some renovations.

563
00:58:39,120 --> 00:58:42,090
Yes, our congregation is growing strongly.

564
00:58:42,760 --> 00:58:47,220
- We need more room. - That was one goddamn hell of a show.

565
00:58:48,370 --> 00:58:50,890
We were happy to have you, Daniel.

566
01:00:44,520 --> 01:00:46,250
Gas, gas, gas!

567
01:00:55,330 --> 01:00:58,420
Lights out! Wait here. Wait here. Lights out!

568
01:01:08,570 --> 01:01:10,370
Put that fire out!

569
01:01:37,240 --> 01:01:41,000
Is he hurt? H.W.! Hand him down to me!

570
01:01:45,580 --> 01:01:47,810
- Hand him down! - Here.

571
01:01:51,950 --> 01:01:54,040
- Got him? - I've got him!

572
01:02:01,360 --> 01:02:02,720
Oh, God.

573
01:02:18,140 --> 01:02:19,540
Come on.

574
01:02:31,690 --> 01:02:33,250
Open the door.

575
01:02:48,070 --> 01:02:50,800
Let go. There you go. You're safe. You're safe.

576
01:02:51,780 --> 01:02:55,610
You're safe now. I got you here. You're safe. Let go, son.

577
01:02:56,980 --> 01:02:59,850
Tell me where it hurts. Tell me where it hurts. Tell me where...

578
01:02:59,980 --> 01:03:01,450
- Did you see this? - No.

579
01:03:01,550 --> 01:03:02,610
Tell me where it hurts.

580
01:03:02,720 --> 01:03:05,280
Where does it hurt you? Where does it hurt you?

581
01:03:05,390 --> 01:03:09,050
- I can't hear my voice. - Were you hit in the head?

582
01:03:09,760 --> 01:03:14,290
Were you hit in the head? Tell me! You have to tell me if you were!

583
01:03:14,400 --> 01:03:16,420
I can't hear my voice.

584
01:03:25,410 --> 01:03:28,140
I have to go and deal with this now. You wait here for me.

585
01:03:28,250 --> 01:03:32,080
You understand? You wait here for me. I'll be back. I'll be back in a minute.

586
01:03:32,180 --> 01:03:33,340
- Wait here. - Don't leave!

587
01:03:33,480 --> 01:03:37,920
I'm going to take care of you. Wait. Stay here, son. I'm going to fix this.

588
01:03:38,020 --> 01:03:38,920
- Don't leave! - You're going to be fine!

589
01:03:39,020 --> 01:03:40,010
Wait for me here!

590
01:03:40,120 --> 01:03:43,120
- Hold him down. Hold him down. - Don't leave!

591
01:03:45,360 --> 01:03:47,990
Got to break the cables, Daniel!

592
01:03:48,130 --> 01:03:50,000
Get me a hammer!

593
01:03:56,310 --> 01:03:58,140
Get me a hammer!

594
01:04:00,710 --> 01:04:02,410
Here you go.

595
01:04:27,740 --> 01:04:29,070
Get back!

596
01:05:06,710 --> 01:05:08,010
- Michael! - Sir!

597
01:05:08,110 --> 01:05:10,550
Take Dave and two of the fellas, pick up some hoses...

598
01:05:10,650 --> 01:05:14,580
Billy, protect the roof. Don't wait before it gets too hot.

599
01:05:36,970 --> 01:05:39,600
What are you looking so miserable about?

600
01:05:39,740 --> 01:05:42,580
There's a whole ocean of oil under our feet!

601
01:05:42,710 --> 01:05:45,380
No one can get at it except for me.

602
01:06:32,100 --> 01:06:33,690
H.W. okay?

603
01:06:34,700 --> 01:06:36,260
No, he isn't.

604
01:06:38,540 --> 01:06:40,870
- Where is he? - Mess room.

605
01:08:20,070 --> 01:08:23,700
That's enough now. That's enough, H.W. That's enough.

606
01:08:26,380 --> 01:08:29,400
Do you hear me? Can you hear me in there?

607
01:08:35,190 --> 01:08:36,880
That's enough.

608
01:08:49,230 --> 01:08:52,000
- Grab his legs. - I have his legs.

609
01:08:52,100 --> 01:08:54,000
- No. Nope. - No, lad.

610
01:08:59,680 --> 01:09:01,340
Give me that.

611
01:09:05,580 --> 01:09:06,640
Steady. That's it.

612
01:09:06,750 --> 01:09:09,150
- Easy, boy. Easy. - Soon be over.

613
01:09:09,250 --> 01:09:13,020
Yeah, and that's good. Now the other side. Turn him over.

614
01:09:16,960 --> 01:09:17,930
Almost done.

615
01:09:21,470 --> 01:09:22,930
That's it.

616
01:09:23,800 --> 01:09:26,600
Come here. It's over. It's over.

617
01:11:32,900 --> 01:11:35,530
Who do we know in San Francisco

618
01:11:37,100 --> 01:11:39,870
or Los Angeles, who could work with...

619
01:11:42,410 --> 01:11:46,140
You know, we could... Someone, a teacher for H.W.

620
01:11:50,480 --> 01:11:52,810
How could you figure out that?

621
01:11:53,680 --> 01:11:57,680
Now, call... God damn it, what's his name?

622
01:11:57,820 --> 01:12:00,120
Bob Brody in San Francisco?

623
01:12:01,290 --> 01:12:04,350
Call Bob Brody and get someone down here.

624
01:12:10,970 --> 01:12:12,870
I'll do it right away.

625
01:13:20,530 --> 01:13:22,790
When do we get our money, Daniel?

626
01:13:28,840 --> 01:13:32,370
Aren't you a healer? And a vessel for the Holy Spirit?

627
01:13:32,510 --> 01:13:35,500
When are you coming over and make my son hear again?

628
01:13:35,650 --> 01:13:36,770
Can't you do that?

629
01:13:36,880 --> 01:13:38,850
lf you had let me bless the well, this wouldn't have happened.

630
01:13:38,980 --> 01:13:41,780
- Daniel. - You shouldn't have done that.

631
01:13:43,150 --> 01:13:47,400
You owe the Church of the Third Revelation $5,000

632
01:13:47,400 --> 01:13:47,450
as part of the arrangement that we made!

633
01:14:00,050 --> 01:14:04,850
Don't even try it, you little runt! You splash around in here.

634
01:14:11,720 --> 01:14:13,620
That's it, that's it.

635
01:14:25,700 --> 01:14:28,370
I'm going to bury you underground, Eli.

636
01:14:32,410 --> 01:14:35,010
I'm going to bury you underground.

637
01:15:06,580 --> 01:15:09,340
You are a stupid man, Abel.

638
01:15:11,180 --> 01:15:15,810
You've let someone come in here and walk all over us.

639
01:15:17,990 --> 01:15:22,450
You let him in and do his work here,

640
01:15:22,560 --> 01:15:26,550
and you are a stupid man for what we could have had.

641
01:15:26,700 --> 01:15:30,640
I followed His word, Eli. I tried.

642
01:15:30,740 --> 01:15:33,470
You didn't do anything but sit down.

643
01:15:34,840 --> 01:15:37,310
You're lazy, and you're stupid.

644
01:15:41,010 --> 01:15:45,140
Do you think God is going to save you for being stupid?

645
01:15:47,820 --> 01:15:50,380
He doesn't save stupid people, Abel.

646
01:15:53,760 --> 01:15:58,200
I will tear you apart for what you've done, you stupid man!

647
01:15:58,330 --> 01:16:00,630
How did he come here? Do you really know? I know!

648
01:16:00,730 --> 01:16:03,360
- Son, don't do this, please! - Be quiet!

649
01:16:03,500 --> 01:16:08,530
Shut your mouth, Abel! lt was your stupid son!

650
01:16:08,670 --> 01:16:12,610
lt was Paul who told him to come here. I know it.

651
01:16:12,710 --> 01:16:14,440
He went to him and he said,

652
01:16:14,550 --> 01:16:19,280
"My stupid, weak father will give away his lots.

653
01:16:19,390 --> 01:16:22,840
"Go and take him." And you let it happen.

654
01:16:27,390 --> 01:16:30,520
A stupid father to a stupid son.

655
01:16:36,170 --> 01:16:37,830
Get out of there!

656
01:17:08,530 --> 01:17:10,160
Can I help you?

657
01:17:11,740 --> 01:17:13,260
Daniel?

658
01:17:13,370 --> 01:17:17,100
- Who's that? - My name is Henry.

659
01:17:18,080 --> 01:17:19,480
Yeah?

660
01:17:20,650 --> 01:17:22,050
I'm Henry.

661
01:17:23,580 --> 01:17:25,610
What can I do for you?

662
01:17:28,490 --> 01:17:32,290
I'm Henry Plainview. I'm from Fond du Lac.

663
01:17:34,830 --> 01:17:38,660
I'm your brother, from another mother.

664
01:17:40,930 --> 01:17:42,830
Ernest is my father.

665
01:17:47,140 --> 01:17:48,660
Who are you?

666
01:17:50,040 --> 01:17:51,270
Henry.

667
01:18:18,340 --> 01:18:22,800
- Mary Branch? Is that your mother? - Yes, sir, that's right.

668
01:18:25,040 --> 01:18:30,210
I read about your gusher in the paper, about your success.

669
01:18:30,350 --> 01:18:33,380
You heard about my strike? You just show up?

670
01:18:34,420 --> 01:18:36,180
Our father's dead.

671
01:18:37,820 --> 01:18:41,020
Ernest died, I heard. I wanted to find you.

672
01:18:41,160 --> 01:18:42,790
When?

673
01:18:42,900 --> 01:18:46,490
Three months ago. I got a letter from Annabelle.

674
01:18:47,500 --> 01:18:49,360
My sister, Annabelle?

675
01:18:51,370 --> 01:18:55,030
- Where is she? - Still at home. Fond du Lac.

676
01:18:56,780 --> 01:19:00,230
You came all the way from Wisconsin to tell me this?

677
01:19:00,380 --> 01:19:03,410
I'm coming from New Mexico. I've been there.

678
01:19:04,620 --> 01:19:06,480
I came to find you.

679
01:19:07,620 --> 01:19:09,680
Did you know about me?

680
01:19:17,800 --> 01:19:19,990
Do you have identification?

681
01:19:20,670 --> 01:19:22,760
Do you have this letter?

682
01:19:45,920 --> 01:19:47,980
- Where are you coming from? - From New Mexico.

683
01:19:48,090 --> 01:19:50,550
Yes, I know, but from where?

684
01:19:50,700 --> 01:19:53,720
Yes, I know, but from where?

685
01:19:51,010 --> 01:19:54,030
Silver City. I've been there for two years.

686
01:19:54,800 --> 01:19:59,600
I was trying drilling of my own for years.

687
01:19:59,740 --> 01:20:06,140
- Getting leases in Texas. Louisiana. - Anything that produced?

688
01:20:06,250 --> 01:20:09,240
No. Not like your success, no.

689
01:20:15,750 --> 01:20:18,190
- Are you married? - No.

690
01:20:18,690 --> 01:20:22,680
I spent time in jail. I had a stretch of very bad time.

691
01:20:23,360 --> 01:20:26,560
I had nothing. I was picked up in Louisiana.

692
01:20:28,070 --> 01:20:31,700
I worked on a chain gang for six months building roads.

693
01:20:32,240 --> 01:20:35,400
That was a very hard time.

694
01:20:39,180 --> 01:20:40,970
Are you married?

695
01:20:42,250 --> 01:20:44,680
What were you in jail for?

696
01:20:44,780 --> 01:20:49,310
Believe it or not, for all the terrible things I've gotten myself into,

697
01:20:49,420 --> 01:20:52,950
when they picked me up, I hadn't done anything.

698
01:20:53,060 --> 01:20:56,860
But I've done my share of things

699
01:20:59,160 --> 01:21:01,560
that shouldn't be talked about.

700
01:21:24,060 --> 01:21:27,120
Drink it. Drink it!

701
01:22:09,700 --> 01:22:11,000
Come on.

702
01:22:42,670 --> 01:22:43,970
So...

703
01:22:48,770 --> 01:22:50,540
What do you want, Henry?

704
01:22:52,980 --> 01:22:54,380
Nothing.

705
01:22:57,520 --> 01:23:01,680
If you can spare something, I can work for you in any way.

706
01:23:01,820 --> 01:23:06,120
I know I'll keep moving, before long, to get back to Fond du Lac.

707
01:23:07,160 --> 01:23:09,490
- Do you have any money? - Some.

708
01:23:10,600 --> 01:23:12,760
- Not much. - Just answer me directly.

709
01:23:12,860 --> 01:23:16,460
You say "nothing," then you say you'd like to stay and work.

710
01:23:16,570 --> 01:23:21,510
And it's better, I'd just like to hear you say you'd like to be here.

711
01:23:22,640 --> 01:23:24,540
I'd like to be here.

712
01:23:29,880 --> 01:23:35,480
I'm a good worker. I worked cable tool rigs, built railroads.

713
01:23:37,660 --> 01:23:39,680
I won't need any favors.

714
01:23:44,700 --> 01:23:45,820
Good.

715
01:24:11,690 --> 01:24:13,850
   What did my mother know?

716
01:24:16,460 --> 01:24:18,120
   I don't know.

717
01:24:18,700 --> 01:24:23,230
   I don't know if she knew and looked the other way, if she never knew.

718
01:24:25,970 --> 01:24:27,730
   Why did you leave?

719
01:24:29,670 --> 01:24:32,640
   I know you didn't get on with our father.

720
01:24:37,850 --> 01:24:41,580
I worked for Geological Survey and went to Kansas.

721
01:24:44,020 --> 01:24:47,050
I couldn't stay there. I just couldn't.

722
01:24:48,790 --> 01:24:51,320
I don't like to explain myself.

723
01:24:57,370 --> 01:25:01,600
- Are you an angry man, Henry? - About what?

724
01:25:02,440 --> 01:25:06,210
Are you envious? Do you get envious?

725
01:25:07,510 --> 01:25:09,450
I don't think so, no.

726
01:25:13,920 --> 01:25:16,250
I have a competition in me.

727
01:25:17,490 --> 01:25:19,890
I want no one else to succeed.

728
01:25:24,930 --> 01:25:29,420
- I hate most people. - That part of me is gone.

729
01:25:30,670 --> 01:25:33,540
Working and not succeeding,

730
01:25:33,640 --> 01:25:37,630
all my failures have left me...

731
01:25:40,680 --> 01:25:42,540
I just don't care.

732
01:25:44,250 --> 01:25:46,840
Well, if it's in me, it's in you.

733
01:25:48,390 --> 01:25:53,790
There are times when I look at people and I see nothing worth liking.

734
01:25:59,800 --> 01:26:03,830
I want to earn enough money I can get away from everyone.

735
01:26:08,870 --> 01:26:11,340
What will you do about your boy?

736
01:26:19,080 --> 01:26:20,710
I don't know.

737
01:26:22,250 --> 01:26:24,690
Maybe it'll change.

738
01:26:24,860 --> 01:26:29,260
Does your sound come back to you? I don't know. Maybe no one knows that.

739
01:26:29,390 --> 01:26:33,560
- Doctor might not know that. - Where's his mother?

740
01:26:39,540 --> 01:26:42,560
I don't want to talk about those things.

741
01:26:45,910 --> 01:26:48,140
I see the worst in people, Henry.

742
01:26:50,180 --> 01:26:54,020
I don't need to look past seeing them to get all I need.

743
01:26:56,190 --> 01:27:00,150
I've built up my hatreds over the years, little by little.

744
01:27:03,860 --> 01:27:07,200
Having you here gives me a second breath of life.

745
01:27:08,430 --> 01:27:11,030
I can't keep doing this on my own

746
01:27:14,340 --> 01:27:19,400
with these people.

747
01:27:59,250 --> 01:28:01,780
Daniel! Daniel, wake up! Daniel!

748
01:29:44,120 --> 01:29:47,580
Just have to go and have a word with the conductor.

749
01:29:48,360 --> 01:29:50,450
I'll be right back.

750
01:29:50,600 --> 01:29:55,290
You stay here. You understand? You stay here.

751
01:29:56,370 --> 01:29:58,200
I'll be right back.

752
01:30:50,920 --> 01:30:52,750
No! No!

753
01:30:54,460 --> 01:30:55,690
No!

754
01:31:05,540 --> 01:31:07,060
- Tilford! - Plainview.

755
01:31:07,210 --> 01:31:09,500
This is my brother, Henry Plainview from Fond du Lac.

756
01:31:09,610 --> 01:31:11,230
H.M. Tilford. Pleasure.

757
01:31:11,380 --> 01:31:13,840
Henry Plainview. J.J. Carter.

758
01:31:15,880 --> 01:31:17,250
So...

759
01:31:17,380 --> 01:31:19,010
- Shall we? - Yes.

760
01:31:27,190 --> 01:31:29,390
How's your boy?

761
01:31:29,530 --> 01:31:32,890
- Thank you for asking. - Is there anything we can do?

762
01:31:33,030 --> 01:31:35,430
Thanks for asking is enough.

763
01:31:37,100 --> 01:31:39,090
So what are your plans?

764
01:31:40,870 --> 01:31:44,100
Is this about buying up my tracts here?

765
01:31:44,240 --> 01:31:45,300
Yes.

766
01:31:45,410 --> 01:31:48,240
The cable was about my Coyote Hills lease.

767
01:31:48,380 --> 01:31:52,540
- We'd like that, too. - What's your offer on Coyote Hills?

768
01:31:52,680 --> 01:31:57,250
- We'll offer 150,000 for full title. - That's a deal. What's next?

769
01:31:58,090 --> 01:32:02,650
You have 11,000 acres in Little Boston. You have one proven well

770
01:32:02,760 --> 01:32:04,250
- that was damaged... - I have three wells proven.

771
01:32:04,400 --> 01:32:08,460
You haven't been paying attention. That's three proven wells.

772
01:32:12,740 --> 01:32:14,640
We'll make you a millionaire while you're sitting here

773
01:32:14,740 --> 01:32:17,070
from one minute to the next.

774
01:32:18,910 --> 01:32:21,670
And what else would I do with myself?

775
01:32:23,410 --> 01:32:27,780
- Are you asking me? - What else would I do with myself?

776
01:32:28,420 --> 01:32:30,510
Take care of your son.

777
01:32:32,190 --> 01:32:34,660
I don't know what you would do.

778
01:32:37,260 --> 01:32:39,730
If you were me and Standard offered to buy what you had

779
01:32:39,860 --> 01:32:42,530
for a million dollars, why? So, why?

780
01:32:43,770 --> 01:32:44,860
You know why.

781
01:32:45,000 --> 01:32:46,830
Yeah, you fellas should just scratch around in the dirt

782
01:32:46,940 --> 01:32:50,370
and find it like the rest of us, instead of buying up someone else's hard work.

783
01:32:50,510 --> 01:32:52,440
I've scratched around the dirt, son.

784
01:32:52,540 --> 01:32:54,530
You going to change your shipping costs?

785
01:32:54,680 --> 01:32:57,650
We don't dictate shipping costs. That's railroad business.

786
01:32:58,680 --> 01:33:01,310
You don't own the railroads?

787
01:33:05,320 --> 01:33:07,880
'Course you do. Of course you do.

788
01:33:09,590 --> 01:33:12,030
Where you going to put it all?

789
01:33:13,060 --> 01:33:14,500
Where?

790
01:33:16,330 --> 01:33:20,330
Build a pipeline? Make a deal with Union Oil? Be my guest.

791
01:33:20,470 --> 01:33:22,130
But if you can't pull it off,

792
01:33:22,240 --> 01:33:26,340
you've got an ocean of oil under your feet with nowhere to go.

793
01:33:27,350 --> 01:33:31,980
Why not turn it over to us? We'll make you rich.

794
01:33:32,120 --> 01:33:34,410
You spend time with your boy.

795
01:33:35,490 --> 01:33:37,610
It's a great discovery.

796
01:33:38,560 --> 01:33:40,650
Now, let us help you.

797
01:33:49,870 --> 01:33:52,960
Did you just tell me how to run my family?

798
01:33:53,100 --> 01:33:55,300
lt might be more important now that you've proven the field

799
01:33:55,440 --> 01:33:57,310
and we're offering to buy you out.

800
01:33:57,440 --> 01:33:59,640
One night I'm going to come to you, inside of your house,

801
01:33:59,780 --> 01:34:02,750
or wherever you're sleeping, and I'm going to cut your throat.

802
01:34:02,850 --> 01:34:04,010
What?

803
01:34:04,780 --> 01:34:06,040
What are you talking about? Have you gone crazy?

804
01:34:06,150 --> 01:34:07,450
- Did you hear what I said? - I heard what you said,

805
01:34:07,590 --> 01:34:10,050
- why did you say it? - You don't tell me about my son.

806
01:34:10,150 --> 01:34:12,350
Why are you acting insane and threatening to cut my throat?

807
01:34:12,460 --> 01:34:15,520
- You don't tell me about my son. - I'm not telling you anything!

808
01:34:15,630 --> 01:34:19,430
I'm asking you to be reasonable. If I've offended you, I apologize.

809
01:34:19,560 --> 01:34:21,730
You'll see what I can do.

810
01:34:29,510 --> 01:34:33,710
This parcel here is the 3,000-acre ranch owned by B.L. Harper.

811
01:34:33,850 --> 01:34:36,340
This is San Luis Obispo County land.

812
01:34:36,480 --> 01:34:38,310
And from here to the coast, it's all Union Oil.

813
01:34:38,420 --> 01:34:41,540
What's this? Why don't I own this?

814
01:34:44,520 --> 01:34:49,050
- Why don't I own this? - That's the Bandy tract.

815
01:34:49,860 --> 01:34:53,020
He was the holdout, when we were doing the buying.

816
01:34:53,130 --> 01:34:55,570
He had hoped to speak with you.

817
01:34:59,770 --> 01:35:03,260
Can't you just build the pipeline around this tract?

818
01:35:06,240 --> 01:35:10,310
Can I build around 50 miles of Tehachapi mountains?

819
01:35:10,450 --> 01:35:12,970
Don't be thick in front of me, Al.

820
01:35:13,620 --> 01:35:17,320
- I can go to him again. - No, I'll go and talk to the man.

821
01:35:17,460 --> 01:35:20,360
I'll talk to him. Show you how it's done.

822
01:35:24,200 --> 01:35:26,630
All right. Pack it up, Henry.

823
01:35:36,970 --> 01:35:40,880
- How big is his room? - He's sharing with another boy.

824
01:35:41,010 --> 01:35:43,850
- Who? - An older boy. About 12.

825
01:35:43,950 --> 01:35:46,970
He's been there for a year. Named Ballard.

826
01:35:52,190 --> 01:35:56,590
- How big is the room? - It's a fair size. Got enough space.

827
01:35:58,900 --> 01:36:02,130
Are you taking Henry with you to meet Union Oil?

828
01:36:15,410 --> 01:36:18,970
- Are you the son of William Bandy? - Grandson.

829
01:36:19,080 --> 01:36:20,850
- Is he here? - No, he's out.

830
01:36:20,990 --> 01:36:22,040
Where is he?

831
01:36:22,190 --> 01:36:25,050
Told you, he's out. Now, what do you want?

832
01:36:28,560 --> 01:36:32,500
I'm Daniel Plainview. I want to talk with him about his property.

833
01:36:32,600 --> 01:36:37,470
- About what? - I believe I'll talk with him about that.

834
01:36:37,940 --> 01:36:40,370
- You're that oilman, aren't you? - That's right.

835
01:36:40,510 --> 01:36:42,470
We don't want you drilling out here.

836
01:36:42,570 --> 01:36:45,970
I don't want it either. Now, when will he be back?

837
01:36:46,080 --> 01:36:47,140
Few days.

838
01:36:47,250 --> 01:36:49,840
Tell him I'd like to speak with him. Not about drilling.

839
01:36:49,950 --> 01:36:52,180
And I'll be back in a week.

840
01:39:11,290 --> 01:39:13,420
Put that in a glass case.

841
01:39:14,330 --> 01:39:16,190
Here's to Union Oil.

842
01:39:16,890 --> 01:39:17,950
Hundred miles of pipeline,

843
01:39:18,100 --> 01:39:20,530
and all the independent producers of this great state.

844
01:39:20,630 --> 01:39:21,600
Cheers.

845
01:39:46,760 --> 01:39:49,450
   There's that house in Fond du Lac

846
01:39:51,360 --> 01:39:54,630
   that John Hollister built. Do you remember it?

847
01:39:57,500 --> 01:40:00,940
I thought as a boy that was the most beautiful house I'd ever seen,

848
01:40:01,040 --> 01:40:02,670
and I wanted it.

849
01:40:03,410 --> 01:40:05,880
I wanted to live in it.

850
01:40:06,010 --> 01:40:07,530
And eat in it.

851
01:40:08,410 --> 01:40:10,000
And clean it.

852
01:40:13,020 --> 01:40:17,320
And even as a boy, I wanted to have children to run around in it.

853
01:40:19,380 --> 01:40:22,110
You can have anything you'd like now, Daniel.

854
01:40:22,820 --> 01:40:24,450
And you should.

855
01:40:25,220 --> 01:40:29,890
- Where are you going to build it? - Here, maybe. Near the ocean.

856
01:40:32,800 --> 01:40:35,560
Would you make it look like that house?

857
01:40:40,300 --> 01:40:43,760
I think if I saw that house now, it'd make me sick.

858
01:40:50,210 --> 01:40:52,680
We can eat and get some women.

859
01:40:55,650 --> 01:40:57,780
Take them to the Peachtree dance.

860
01:41:01,530 --> 01:41:05,460
I say get liquored up and take them to the Peachtree dance.

861
01:41:08,370 --> 01:41:09,590
Yeah.

862
01:42:28,550 --> 01:42:30,950
Can I have some money, please?

863
01:42:38,360 --> 01:42:40,760
Can I have some money, please?

864
01:43:29,840 --> 01:43:32,330
I want you to tell me something.

865
01:43:36,010 --> 01:43:37,170
What?

866
01:43:38,220 --> 01:43:41,670
What's the name of the farm next to the Hill House?

867
01:43:52,730 --> 01:43:57,390
What was the name of the farm next to the Hill House?

868
01:44:00,940 --> 01:44:03,930
- I can't remember... - Who are you?

869
01:44:06,880 --> 01:44:08,780
I'll leave, Daniel.

870
01:44:10,550 --> 01:44:12,110
Who are you?

871
01:44:15,450 --> 01:44:16,980
I'm no one.

872
01:44:18,060 --> 01:44:20,320
Just let me get up and go.

873
01:44:22,830 --> 01:44:24,690
Do I have a brother?

874
01:44:28,670 --> 01:44:33,860
I met a man in King City who said he was your brother.

875
01:44:36,410 --> 01:44:39,500
We were friends for months.

876
01:44:40,980 --> 01:44:42,910
Working in King City.

877
01:44:45,150 --> 01:44:48,020
And he wanted to make his way to you, Daniel.

878
01:44:49,290 --> 01:44:51,410
We didn't have any money.

879
01:44:56,290 --> 01:44:58,560
He died of tuberculosis.

880
01:45:00,000 --> 01:45:01,830
He wasn't harmed.

881
01:45:02,870 --> 01:45:05,100
Wasn't killed, nothing bad.

882
01:45:06,940 --> 01:45:09,200
But he told me about you,

883
01:45:12,240 --> 01:45:14,540
and I just took his story,

884
01:45:18,250 --> 01:45:20,050
used his diary.

885
01:45:23,690 --> 01:45:24,650
Daniel.

886
01:45:26,290 --> 01:45:29,620
Daniel, I'm your friend.

887
01:45:31,830 --> 01:45:34,260
I'm not trying to hurt you.

888
01:45:34,400 --> 01:45:35,630
Never.

889
01:45:36,770 --> 01:45:38,290
Just survive.

890
01:45:38,840 --> 01:45:40,060
No!

891
01:48:49,690 --> 01:48:51,160
Who is it?

892
01:48:52,460 --> 01:48:53,930
I'm Bandy.

893
01:49:06,710 --> 01:49:08,580
Yes. Yes.

894
01:49:11,080 --> 01:49:12,810
William Bandy.

895
01:49:16,020 --> 01:49:18,650
Yeah, I'd like to lease your land.

896
01:49:21,090 --> 01:49:24,650
I had asked for you to come and talk to me before.

897
01:49:24,760 --> 01:49:27,030
When you were leasing land.

898
01:49:28,260 --> 01:49:30,060
That's right, yes.

899
01:49:31,770 --> 01:49:34,290
My boy's been very sick, you know.

900
01:49:35,440 --> 01:49:37,960
This was before your boy got sick.

901
01:49:41,080 --> 01:49:45,610
Now, I know that you would like to build a pipeline

902
01:49:45,750 --> 01:49:48,410
through my property.

903
01:49:48,520 --> 01:49:52,650
- Is that right, what I've heard? - It's absolutely right. And,

904
01:49:53,360 --> 01:49:54,320
well...

905
01:49:55,630 --> 01:49:58,860
Eight inch pipe. It could be buried with your consent.

906
01:49:59,000 --> 01:50:01,520
I guarantee you absolutely no disruption...

907
01:50:01,670 --> 01:50:02,830
God.

908
01:50:04,700 --> 01:50:07,330
God has told me what you must do.

909
01:50:11,710 --> 01:50:13,440
And what is that?

910
01:50:14,410 --> 01:50:18,310
You should be washed in the blood of Jesus Christ.

911
01:50:20,120 --> 01:50:22,050
But I am.

912
01:50:23,590 --> 01:50:26,280
I have been washed, Mr. Bandy. I have been.

913
01:50:26,420 --> 01:50:32,120
It's your only way to salvation. And your only way for what you want.

914
01:50:33,960 --> 01:50:37,520
You can take it at the Church of the Third Revelation.

915
01:50:39,970 --> 01:50:41,940
I'll pay you $3,000.

916
01:50:44,570 --> 01:50:47,340
I'd like you to be part of our church.

917
01:50:49,250 --> 01:50:51,150
I'll pay you $5,000.

918
01:50:52,250 --> 01:50:53,720
Be baptized.

919
01:50:55,090 --> 01:50:58,920
Be forgiven for the sin that you've done.

920
01:51:03,190 --> 01:51:08,060
What sin are you referring to, Mr. Bandy?

921
01:51:09,230 --> 01:51:11,130
My sin of drilling?

922
01:52:01,820 --> 01:52:05,810
   I truly wish everyone could be saved, don't you?

923
01:52:05,960 --> 01:52:07,860
   Yes.

924
01:52:07,990 --> 01:52:10,690
   I am afraid that's just not the case.

925
01:52:11,560 --> 01:52:16,060
The doctrine of universal salvation is a lie, is it not?

926
01:52:16,200 --> 01:52:18,830
- It's a lie. - It's a lie.

927
01:52:18,940 --> 01:52:23,700
I wish everyone could be saved, but they won't. No, they won't.

928
01:52:23,840 --> 01:52:27,300
You will never be saved if you...

929
01:52:27,410 --> 01:52:29,380
Reject the blood.

930
01:52:30,210 --> 01:52:31,370
Good.

931
01:52:32,450 --> 01:52:36,910
Now, is there a sinner here looking for salvation?

932
01:52:39,590 --> 01:52:41,180
A new member?

933
01:52:45,660 --> 01:52:47,430
I'll ask it again.

934
01:52:49,430 --> 01:52:52,130
Is there a sinner here looking for God?

935
01:52:52,270 --> 01:52:53,430
Yes.

936
01:52:57,540 --> 01:52:58,970
Allow me.

937
01:53:01,210 --> 01:53:03,980
Thank you for coming, brother Daniel.

938
01:53:06,080 --> 01:53:07,740
Thank you, Eli.

939
01:53:08,890 --> 01:53:13,980
We have a sinner with us here who wishes for salvation!

940
01:53:14,090 --> 01:53:17,690
- Daniel, are you a sinner? - Yes.

941
01:53:17,790 --> 01:53:20,490
The Lord can't hear you, Daniel.

942
01:53:20,600 --> 01:53:24,430
Say it to him. Go ahead and speak to him. It's all right.

943
01:53:25,240 --> 01:53:27,530
- Yes. - Down on your knees.

944
01:53:27,640 --> 01:53:29,200
Pray to him.

945
01:53:30,610 --> 01:53:34,980
Look up to the sky and say it.

946
01:53:37,580 --> 01:53:39,740
What do you want me to say?

947
01:53:40,780 --> 01:53:45,280
Daniel, you've come here and you've brought good and wealth,

948
01:53:45,390 --> 01:53:49,590
but you have also brought your bad habits as a backslider.

949
01:53:49,690 --> 01:53:53,960
You've lusted after women, and you have abandoned your child.

950
01:53:54,060 --> 01:53:57,120
Your child, that you raised, you have abandoned

951
01:53:57,230 --> 01:53:59,670
all because he was sick and you have sinned.

952
01:53:59,800 --> 01:54:01,960
So say it now. I am a sinner.

953
01:54:02,070 --> 01:54:03,970
- I am a sinner. - Say it louder.

954
01:54:04,070 --> 01:54:06,800
- I am a sinner. - I am a sinner.

955
01:54:06,940 --> 01:54:08,840
Louder, Daniel! I am a sinner!

956
01:54:08,980 --> 01:54:11,910
- I am a sinner. - I am sorry, Lord.

957
01:54:12,020 --> 01:54:14,180
- I am sorry, Lord. - I want the blood.

958
01:54:14,320 --> 01:54:17,680
- I want the blood. - You have abandoned your child.

959
01:54:18,450 --> 01:54:19,750
I have abandoned my child.

960
01:54:19,860 --> 01:54:22,190
- I will never backslide. - I will never backslide.

961
01:54:22,330 --> 01:54:25,320
I was lost, but now I am found.

962
01:54:25,460 --> 01:54:29,360
- I was lost, but now I'm found. - I have abandoned my child.

963
01:54:31,130 --> 01:54:34,300
Say it. Say it.

964
01:54:34,400 --> 01:54:37,430
- I abandoned my child. - Say it louder. Say it louder!

965
01:54:37,540 --> 01:54:39,630
I've abandoned my child!

966
01:54:40,540 --> 01:54:43,070
I've abandoned my child!

967
01:54:43,210 --> 01:54:45,200
I've abandoned my boy!

968
01:54:45,350 --> 01:54:47,750
Now beg for the blood!

969
01:54:48,950 --> 01:54:50,820
Just give me the blood, Eli. Let me get out of here.

970
01:54:50,920 --> 01:54:53,680
Give me the blood, Lord, and let me get away!

971
01:54:53,790 --> 01:54:57,560
Do you accept Jesus Christ as your Lord and Savior?

972
01:54:57,690 --> 01:55:00,420
- Yes, I do. - Get out of here, devil!

973
01:55:00,560 --> 01:55:03,360
Out, devil! Out, sin!

974
01:55:03,530 --> 01:55:06,060
- Let me feel the power of the Lord, Eli. - Do you accept

975
01:55:06,200 --> 01:55:10,070
the Church of the Third Revelation as your spiritual guide?

976
01:55:11,610 --> 01:55:15,810
- Get out of here, ghost! - Where is your Lord, Eli?

977
01:55:15,950 --> 01:55:20,010
- Get out! Go back where you belong! - Where is he? There he is!

978
01:55:20,150 --> 01:55:23,740
Do you accept Jesus Christ as your Savior?

979
01:55:23,850 --> 01:55:25,290
Yes, I do.

980
01:55:28,060 --> 01:55:32,360
   Would you be free from the burden of sin?

981
01:55:32,500 --> 01:55:34,830
   There's power in the blood

982
01:55:34,960 --> 01:55:36,990
   Power in the blood

983
01:55:37,270 --> 01:55:39,060
   Would you o'er evil a victory win?

984
01:55:39,170 --> 01:55:41,360
There's a pipeline.

985
01:55:41,500 --> 01:55:45,670
   There's wonderful power in the blood

986
01:55:45,810 --> 01:55:50,180
   There is power, power wonder-working power

987
01:55:50,280 --> 01:55:53,980
   In the blood of the Lamb

988
01:55:54,080 --> 01:55:55,850
Praise the Lord!

989
01:56:00,460 --> 01:56:03,320
Welcome to the fold, brother Plainview.

990
01:56:14,670 --> 01:56:16,930
Welcome, brother Daniel. God bless you.

991
01:56:18,210 --> 01:56:19,640
God bless you.

992
01:56:22,810 --> 01:56:24,470
- Hallelujah. - Amen.

993
01:56:24,910 --> 01:56:26,850
Welcome home, brother.

994
01:56:27,480 --> 01:56:30,940
That's enough. That's enough, now.

995
01:56:33,190 --> 01:56:37,350
He must take the spirit in on his own.

996
01:56:40,130 --> 01:56:41,990
We have a new member.

997
01:56:42,130 --> 01:56:44,260
- Yes, brother. - Hallelujah.

998
01:56:44,370 --> 01:56:46,340
- Hallelujah. - Amen.

999
01:56:48,500 --> 01:56:50,600
- My sweet Mary. - Mr. Plainview has been generous

1000
01:56:50,710 --> 01:56:53,440
enough to make a $5,000 donation

1001
01:56:53,580 --> 01:56:56,600
to the church which we are still waiting for.

1002
01:58:08,750 --> 01:58:12,050
That does me good. That does me good.

1003
01:58:14,160 --> 01:58:15,990
Welcome home, son.

1004
01:58:18,590 --> 01:58:20,560
Welcome home, son.

1005
01:58:24,500 --> 01:58:26,560
This here's George Reynolds. Teacher from the deaf school.

1006
01:58:26,670 --> 01:58:29,660
- Mr. Plainview. - Fletcher.

1007
01:58:32,480 --> 01:58:34,570
You're too heavy for me.

1008
01:58:37,650 --> 01:58:40,340
Do you want to get something to eat?

1009
01:58:41,550 --> 01:58:45,850
That's the pipeline, see? All the way to the sea.

1010
01:59:06,980 --> 01:59:08,530
Come here.

1011
01:59:15,420 --> 01:59:17,180
I love you, son.

1012
01:59:19,090 --> 01:59:21,220
Let's take a look at you.

1013
01:59:23,490 --> 01:59:26,360
All right. That's it, that's it. That's it.

1014
01:59:50,420 --> 01:59:53,720
Let's get some decent food inside of you.

1015
01:59:53,820 --> 01:59:57,620
That's all we need here is a good, strong, expensive meal.

1016
01:59:58,260 --> 01:59:59,750
You hungry?

1017
02:00:00,830 --> 02:00:01,920
- Waiter? - Yes, sir.

1018
02:00:02,060 --> 02:00:05,060
Two steaks, a whiskey, and water for him.

1019
02:00:06,700 --> 02:00:09,230
- And goat's milk. - Very good, sir.

1020
02:00:16,050 --> 02:00:18,980
We're going to have this teacher help you.

1021
02:00:19,550 --> 02:00:24,010
He's going to help take care of all of this. Understand?

1022
02:00:24,150 --> 02:00:26,850
'Cause I need you. Need your help.

1023
02:00:26,990 --> 02:00:30,950
Got everything we need now to build this company. Come here.

1024
02:00:38,770 --> 02:00:40,460
Good afternoon.

1025
02:00:56,620 --> 02:00:58,680
- How are you doing? - It's nice to see you again.

1026
02:00:58,790 --> 02:01:01,590
- We need four. - I'll have them right up.

1027
02:01:05,760 --> 02:01:07,750
- Good afternoon, Daniel. - Tilford.

1028
02:01:07,860 --> 02:01:09,230
Good afternoon.

1029
02:01:10,800 --> 02:01:16,070
- Hello! H.M. Tilford! - You don't have to shout.

1030
02:01:18,110 --> 02:01:19,510
Pleasure.

1031
02:01:24,210 --> 02:01:26,480
It's good to be in Little B.

1032
02:01:27,750 --> 02:01:31,050
- Could use some rain out here. - Yeah, we could.

1033
02:01:31,920 --> 02:01:35,020
- There we go. - R.J., how's the London broil?

1034
02:01:35,160 --> 02:01:37,820
Believe we ordered these drinks before those people.

1035
02:01:37,930 --> 02:01:42,190
- R.J., tell us. How's the London broil? - Excuse me, gentlemen. Sorry.

1036
02:01:44,270 --> 02:01:48,200
I am sorry about that, sir. I'll have your steaks right out.

1037
02:01:58,050 --> 02:02:00,610
- So that green turtle soup is fantastic. - Is it?

1038
02:02:00,750 --> 02:02:02,380
lt's delicious.

1039
02:02:07,420 --> 02:02:08,390
Sounds good to me.

1040
02:02:08,520 --> 02:02:14,260
So Standard offered us a million dollars for the Little Boston leases.

1041
02:02:14,360 --> 02:02:17,260
I told H.M. Tilford where he could shove that.

1042
02:02:17,370 --> 02:02:21,960
And we made a deal with Union! On the pipeline!

1043
02:02:22,100 --> 02:02:25,560
And that whole ocean of oil underneath our fields.

1044
02:02:25,670 --> 02:02:27,340
...$150,000. - Yes.

1045
02:02:27,440 --> 02:02:29,740
We needed the money to drill.

1046
02:02:29,880 --> 02:02:32,110
- Who is this guy? - I go out to meet him.

1047
02:02:32,210 --> 02:02:34,980
He's getting oil on the property. We're trying to make a claim on it.

1048
02:02:35,120 --> 02:02:37,020
Offered him a million dollars.

1049
02:02:37,150 --> 02:02:40,350
- Turned us down flat. - Well, I'm hungry.

1050
02:02:40,490 --> 02:02:45,120
Orange fritters, mashed potatoes, green peas.

1051
02:02:45,230 --> 02:02:47,700
- All the way around? - All right.

1052
02:02:50,600 --> 02:02:51,960
Hold on.

1053
02:02:55,740 --> 02:02:58,000
I want you to look over there.

1054
02:02:58,110 --> 02:03:00,910
- Daniel, let me introduce... - Look over there. You see?

1055
02:03:01,040 --> 02:03:03,140
That's my son. See him?

1056
02:03:03,250 --> 02:03:05,580
- Yes. - Do you see?

1057
02:03:07,920 --> 02:03:09,350
I see him.

1058
02:03:10,220 --> 02:03:13,090
You don't tell me how to raise my family.

1059
02:03:15,220 --> 02:03:18,750
I told you not to tell me how to raise my family.

1060
02:03:20,230 --> 02:03:22,090
Daniel...

1061
02:03:22,930 --> 02:03:24,760
So what do you see?

1062
02:03:26,770 --> 02:03:29,930
- I'm very happy for you that the deal... - Yes, I made a deal with Union.

1063
02:03:30,040 --> 02:03:32,410
- My son is happy. He's safe. - Congratulations.

1064
02:03:32,510 --> 02:03:35,670
- I'm taking care of him now, so... - Excellent.

1065
02:03:36,980 --> 02:03:39,970
You look like a fool, don't you, Tilford?

1066
02:03:44,650 --> 02:03:47,490
- Yes. - Yes.

1067
02:03:49,330 --> 02:03:50,990
Yes, you do.

1068
02:03:51,890 --> 02:03:53,360
Excuse me, gentlemen.

1069
02:03:53,700 --> 02:03:56,930
Excuse me, gentlemen. Excuse him, gentlemen.

1070
02:04:00,470 --> 02:04:03,100
I told you what I was going to do.

1071
02:04:13,420 --> 02:04:14,640
My son.

1072
02:04:32,700 --> 02:04:36,000
Mr. Sunday, I understand that you're leaving our fair community.

1073
02:04:36,140 --> 02:04:39,270
- Yes, I'm going on a mission. - Where you going?

1074
02:04:39,380 --> 02:04:41,540
Oildale, Taft, and then on to Bakersfield.

1075
02:04:41,680 --> 02:04:44,010
Well, I want you to know...

1076
02:04:44,150 --> 02:04:46,010
Three quarters of an hour.

1077
02:04:46,150 --> 02:04:47,670
...you done a great job for us.

1078
02:04:47,820 --> 02:04:50,680
- Thank you. You will be in my prayers. - I thank you very much.

1079
02:04:50,790 --> 02:04:54,050
Union Oil Company, Santa Paula, California.

1080
02:07:03,050 --> 02:07:05,090
"The woman saith unto him, 'Sir, give me this water

1081
02:07:06,850 --> 02:07:07,890
"'and I shall thirst not, neither come hither to draw."'

1082
02:08:54,360 --> 02:08:56,020
Come in, come in.

1083
02:09:22,790 --> 02:09:25,020
Can we be alone?

1084
02:09:25,130 --> 02:09:28,820
This is my closest associate. He hears everything.

1085
02:09:35,900 --> 02:09:40,970
- I'd prefer to speak to you in private. - You can't speak.

1086
02:09:41,080 --> 02:09:43,310
So why don't you flap your hands about

1087
02:09:43,410 --> 02:09:46,970
and have what's-his-name tell me where you've been.

1088
02:09:54,960 --> 02:09:57,690
Or do you think I don't know?

1089
02:10:12,170 --> 02:10:14,400
This is hard for me to say.

1090
02:10:15,510 --> 02:10:19,640
I'll tell you first, I love you very much.

1091
02:10:22,920 --> 02:10:26,910
I've learned to love what I do because of you.

1092
02:10:30,360 --> 02:10:32,220
I'm leaving here.

1093
02:10:33,660 --> 02:10:35,990
I'm going to Mexico.

1094
02:10:36,130 --> 02:10:39,100
I'm taking Mary, and I'm going to Mexico.

1095
02:10:40,770 --> 02:10:42,860
I miss working outside.

1096
02:10:43,910 --> 02:10:45,770
I miss the fields.

1097
02:10:48,740 --> 02:10:50,870
It'll only be for a time,

1098
02:10:52,080 --> 02:10:54,410
for me to do my own drilling

1099
02:10:56,120 --> 02:10:58,250
and start my own company.

1100
02:11:01,260 --> 02:11:05,720
It's time to make a change.

1101
02:11:18,770 --> 02:11:21,270
This makes you my competitor.

1102
02:11:25,250 --> 02:11:30,340
- No. No, it's not like that. - It is like that, boy.

1103
02:11:31,590 --> 02:11:33,550
Your own company, huh?

1104
02:11:33,990 --> 02:11:35,480
That's right.

1105
02:11:37,830 --> 02:11:39,590
In Mexico?

1106
02:11:41,060 --> 02:11:42,120
Yes.

1107
02:11:42,230 --> 02:11:47,290
You are making such a misstep. So, what are you doing?

1108
02:11:49,340 --> 02:11:52,670
I know you and I have disagreed over many things.

1109
02:11:53,610 --> 02:11:57,940
I'd rather keep you as my father than my partner.

1110
02:11:58,050 --> 02:11:59,510
Then say it.

1111
02:11:59,650 --> 02:12:01,340
If you've got something to say to me, then say it.

1112
02:12:01,450 --> 02:12:05,110
I'd like to hear you speak instead of your little dog.

1113
02:12:23,240 --> 02:12:25,900
I'm going to Mexico with my wife.

1114
02:12:26,910 --> 02:12:29,040
I'm going away from you.

1115
02:12:35,080 --> 02:12:37,750
That wasn't so hard, was it?

1116
02:12:39,690 --> 02:12:42,320
Killing us with what you're doing.

1117
02:12:45,230 --> 02:12:48,690
You're killing my image of you as my son.

1118
02:12:48,830 --> 02:12:52,200
You are stubborn. You won't listen.

1119
02:12:52,330 --> 02:12:54,630
You're not my son.

1120
02:12:54,740 --> 02:12:57,930
Please don't say that. I know you don't mean it.

1121
02:12:58,040 --> 02:13:02,000
It's the truth. You're not my son. You never have been.

1122
02:13:03,380 --> 02:13:05,180
You're an orphan!

1123
02:13:07,880 --> 02:13:10,110
Did you ever hear that word?

1124
02:13:11,620 --> 02:13:13,520
Tell him what I said.

1125
02:13:14,290 --> 02:13:17,260
You operated here today like one.

1126
02:13:18,890 --> 02:13:21,360
I should have seen this coming.

1127
02:13:22,860 --> 02:13:27,700
I should have known that, under this all, these past years

1128
02:13:27,840 --> 02:13:31,200
you've been building new hate for me, piece by piece.

1129
02:13:31,340 --> 02:13:34,970
I don't even know who you are because you have none of me in you.

1130
02:13:35,080 --> 02:13:37,940
You're someone else's.

1131
02:13:39,380 --> 02:13:42,840
This anger. Your maliciousness.

1132
02:13:43,950 --> 02:13:46,850
Backwards dealings with me.

1133
02:13:48,520 --> 02:13:52,480
You're an orphan from a basket in the middle of the desert.

1134
02:13:55,300 --> 02:14:00,260
And I took you for no other reason than I needed a sweet face to buy land.

1135
02:14:01,770 --> 02:14:03,530
Did you get that?

1136
02:14:04,770 --> 02:14:06,540
So now you know.

1137
02:14:09,850 --> 02:14:14,150
Look at me! You're lower than a bastard.

1138
02:14:39,110 --> 02:14:43,570
You have none of me in you. You're just a bastard from a basket.

1139
02:14:53,260 --> 02:14:57,520
I thank God I have none of you in me.

1140
02:15:02,430 --> 02:15:06,890
Not my son. Just a little piece of competition.

1141
02:15:08,800 --> 02:15:10,900
Bastard from a basket.

1142
02:15:13,310 --> 02:15:15,500
Bastard from a basket!

1143
02:15:23,890 --> 02:15:26,410
You're a bastard from a basket!

1144
02:16:28,950 --> 02:16:30,750
   Get up, Mr. Daniel.

1145
02:16:35,120 --> 02:16:36,680
   Mr. Daniel.

1146
02:16:38,660 --> 02:16:41,220
Mr. Daniel, you've got a visitor.

1147
02:16:44,900 --> 02:16:46,730
Wake up, Mr. Daniel.

1148
02:16:49,470 --> 02:16:51,060
Sir?

1149
02:17:04,590 --> 02:17:06,520
You can leave us now.

1150
02:17:14,830 --> 02:17:15,800
Daniel.

1151
02:17:19,170 --> 02:17:20,330
Daniel.

1152
02:17:22,940 --> 02:17:26,130
Daniel Plainview, the house is on fire!

1153
02:17:30,810 --> 02:17:33,780
Brother Daniel, it's Eli.

1154
02:17:44,030 --> 02:17:47,760
Yes, it is. Yes, it is.

1155
02:17:49,860 --> 02:17:51,800
I'll make us a drink.

1156
02:17:58,370 --> 02:18:01,540
Your home is a miracle.

1157
02:18:02,810 --> 02:18:04,080
It's beautiful.

1158
02:18:04,080 --> 02:18:04,440
It's beautiful.

1159
02:18:05,080 --> 02:18:07,140
God bless it.

1160
02:18:07,280 --> 02:18:11,280
I've been spreading His word far and wide.

1161
02:18:12,550 --> 02:18:14,350
Far and wide.

1162
02:18:16,160 --> 02:18:18,920
So much travel for Him.

1163
02:18:23,630 --> 02:18:26,030
I've been working in radio.

1164
02:18:28,740 --> 02:18:32,700
Yes, so much... So much has been happening.

1165
02:18:33,740 --> 02:18:39,200
To be here and find you and see you well is wonderful.

1166
02:18:39,350 --> 02:18:41,910
And we have a chance to catch up.

1167
02:18:55,060 --> 02:18:57,120
No. Thank you so much.

1168
02:19:15,250 --> 02:19:16,770
My brother.

1169
02:19:18,190 --> 02:19:21,450
Daniel, my brother by marriage.

1170
02:19:23,460 --> 02:19:27,550
We're such old friends. So much time.

1171
02:19:34,070 --> 02:19:37,160
Things go up, things go down,

1172
02:19:37,270 --> 02:19:41,570
but at least the Lord is always around.

1173
02:19:43,180 --> 02:19:45,840
We've seen ups and downs, haven't we?

1174
02:19:49,650 --> 02:19:52,620
Are things down for you right now, Eli?

1175
02:19:53,990 --> 02:19:55,390
No. No.

1176
02:19:57,830 --> 02:20:00,450
But I do come with some sad news.

1177
02:20:02,200 --> 02:20:04,930
Perhaps you remember Mr. Bandy?

1178
02:20:07,570 --> 02:20:10,900
Mr. Bandy has passed on to the Lord.

1179
02:20:11,840 --> 02:20:15,000
He lived to be 99 years old, God bless him.

1180
02:20:15,710 --> 02:20:19,580
Mr. Bandy has a grandson. Have you met his grandson, William?

1181
02:20:20,580 --> 02:20:25,180
William Bandy is one of the finest members we have

1182
02:20:25,290 --> 02:20:27,850
at the Church of the Third Revelation.

1183
02:20:27,960 --> 02:20:31,260
He's eager to come to Hollywood to be in movies.

1184
02:20:32,730 --> 02:20:34,890
He is very good-looking.

1185
02:20:37,100 --> 02:20:42,090
- And I do think he will have success. - That's wonderful.

1186
02:20:44,240 --> 02:20:47,000
Would you like me to speak with him?

1187
02:20:54,420 --> 02:20:59,150
Daniel, I'm asking if you'd like to have business

1188
02:20:59,290 --> 02:21:01,520
with the Church of the Third Revelation

1189
02:21:01,620 --> 02:21:05,860
in developing this lease on young Bandy's 1,000-acre tract.

1190
02:21:08,330 --> 02:21:09,920
I'm offering you to drill

1191
02:21:10,060 --> 02:21:13,520
on one of the great undeveloped fields of Little Boston.

1192
02:21:13,640 --> 02:21:17,770
- I'd be happy to work with you. - You would?

1193
02:21:19,370 --> 02:21:22,210
Yes, yes, of course. That's wonderful.

1194
02:21:22,340 --> 02:21:25,310
But there is one condition for this work.

1195
02:21:25,410 --> 02:21:26,900
All right.

1196
02:21:28,980 --> 02:21:32,510
I'd like you to tell me that you are a false prophet.

1197
02:21:37,890 --> 02:21:43,300
I'd like you to tell me that you are, and have been a false prophet.

1198
02:21:44,500 --> 02:21:46,870
And that God is a superstition.

1199
02:21:52,970 --> 02:21:54,770
But that's a lie.

1200
02:21:57,580 --> 02:22:00,100
It's a lie. I cannot say it.

1201
02:22:14,400 --> 02:22:16,830
- When can we begin to drill? - Very soon.

1202
02:22:16,930 --> 02:22:18,520
How long will it take to bring in the well?

1203
02:22:18,670 --> 02:22:20,570
lt shouldn't take long.

1204
02:22:20,700 --> 02:22:23,970
I would like a $100,000 signing bonus,

1205
02:22:24,070 --> 02:22:27,340
plus the five that is owed to me with interest.

1206
02:22:28,040 --> 02:22:29,810
That's only fair.

1207
02:22:35,580 --> 02:22:40,350
I am a false prophet, and God is a superstition.

1208
02:22:40,490 --> 02:22:43,460
If that's what you believe, then I will say it.

1209
02:22:43,560 --> 02:22:47,050
- Say it like you mean it. - Daniel.

1210
02:22:47,600 --> 02:22:49,930
Say it like it's your sermon.

1211
02:22:53,100 --> 02:22:54,730
Don't smile.

1212
02:23:00,510 --> 02:23:02,410
I am a false prophet.

1213
02:23:02,510 --> 02:23:05,840
- God is a superstition. - Why don't you stand up?

1214
02:23:08,920 --> 02:23:10,910
Put your glass down.

1215
02:23:23,100 --> 02:23:26,660
I am a false prophet.

1216
02:23:26,800 --> 02:23:29,860
- God is a superstition. - Eli, stop.

1217
02:23:29,970 --> 02:23:35,380
Just imagine this is your church here and you have a full congregation, so...

1218
02:23:37,910 --> 02:23:41,680
I am a false prophet. God is a superstition.

1219
02:23:41,780 --> 02:23:43,380
Say it again.

1220
02:23:44,450 --> 02:23:48,320
I am a false prophet. God is a superstition.

1221
02:23:48,420 --> 02:23:49,550
They can't hear you at the back.

1222
02:23:49,690 --> 02:23:53,060
I am a false prophet. God is a superstition.

1223
02:23:53,190 --> 02:23:54,220
Say it again.

1224
02:23:54,360 --> 02:23:58,990
I am a false prophet! God is a superstition!

1225
02:23:59,100 --> 02:24:00,800
Say it again.

1226
02:24:00,900 --> 02:24:04,630
I am a false prophet! God is a superstition!

1227
02:24:05,840 --> 02:24:08,170
Those areas have been drilled.

1228
02:24:11,280 --> 02:24:12,680
What?

1229
02:24:12,810 --> 02:24:15,410
Those areas, they've been drilled.

1230
02:24:17,020 --> 02:24:20,550
- No, they haven't. - Yes, it's...

1231
02:24:20,660 --> 02:24:21,990
It's called drainage, Eli.

1232
02:24:22,120 --> 02:24:26,960
See, I own everything around it, so, of course, I get what's underneath it.

1233
02:24:28,430 --> 02:24:31,590
But there are no derricks there.

1234
02:24:31,730 --> 02:24:34,100
This is the Bandy tract. Do you understand?

1235
02:24:34,240 --> 02:24:36,200
Do you understand, Eli?

1236
02:24:36,940 --> 02:24:40,170
That's more to the point. Do you understand?

1237
02:24:40,270 --> 02:24:45,680
I drink your water. I drink it up every day.

1238
02:24:46,680 --> 02:24:50,910
I drink the blood of Lamb from Bandy's tract.

1239
02:24:56,190 --> 02:24:58,280
You can sit down again.

1240
02:25:16,440 --> 02:25:17,780
Daniel.

1241
02:25:21,050 --> 02:25:22,040
Daniel.

1242
02:25:25,920 --> 02:25:27,220
Please.

1243
02:25:29,860 --> 02:25:34,190
- I am in desperate times. - I know.

1244
02:25:34,300 --> 02:25:37,160
- I need a friend. - Yes. Of course, you do.

1245
02:25:37,570 --> 02:25:39,160
I've sinned.

1246
02:25:40,940 --> 02:25:44,030
I need help. I'm a sinner.

1247
02:25:44,170 --> 02:25:48,770
I've let the devil grab hold of me in ways I never imagined.

1248
02:25:48,880 --> 02:25:50,310
I'm so full of sin.

1249
02:25:50,410 --> 02:25:53,680
The Lord sometimes challenges us, doesn't He, Eli?

1250
02:25:53,820 --> 02:25:55,780
- Yes, He does, Daniel. - Yes, He does.

1251
02:25:55,880 --> 02:25:58,480
Yes, He does!

1252
02:25:58,620 --> 02:26:00,520
Yes, He does!

1253
02:26:01,820 --> 02:26:07,390
He's completely failed to alert me to the recent panic in our economy.

1254
02:26:07,500 --> 02:26:09,660
- And this... - Oh, dear.

1255
02:26:09,800 --> 02:26:16,460
I must have this, Daniel. I must, I must, I must have this.

1256
02:26:16,600 --> 02:26:18,870
My investments have...

1257
02:26:18,970 --> 02:26:24,000
Daniel, I won't bore you, but if I could grab the Lord's hand for help I would,

1258
02:26:24,110 --> 02:26:27,010
but He does these things all the time.

1259
02:26:27,110 --> 02:26:31,070
These mysteries that He presents, and while we wait...

1260
02:26:32,350 --> 02:26:34,510
While we wait for His word!

1261
02:26:34,660 --> 02:26:37,620
Because you're not the chosen brother, Eli.

1262
02:26:37,340 --> 02:26:37,570
Because you're not the chosen brother, Eli.

1263
02:26:40,030 --> 02:26:43,830
'Twas Paul who was chosen.

1264
02:26:44,730 --> 02:26:47,670
He found me and told me about your land. You're just a fool.

1265
02:26:47,800 --> 02:26:50,640
- Why are you talking about Paul? - I did what your brother couldn't.

1266
02:26:50,740 --> 02:26:53,260
- Don't say this to me. - I broke you and I beat you.

1267
02:26:54,180 --> 02:26:56,970
It was Paul told me about you.

1268
02:26:57,110 --> 02:27:01,570
He's the prophet. He's the smart one. He knew what was there

1269
02:27:01,680 --> 02:27:04,050
and he found me to take it out of the ground.

1270
02:27:04,150 --> 02:27:07,250
Know what the funny thing is? Listen, listen.

1271
02:27:08,120 --> 02:27:12,020
I paid him $10,000 cash in hand. Just like that.

1272
02:27:13,060 --> 02:27:16,390
He has his own company now. Prosperous little business.

1273
02:27:16,500 --> 02:27:20,020
Three wells producing, $5,000 a week.

1274
02:27:22,100 --> 02:27:25,900
Stop crying, you sniveling ass. Stop your nonsense.

1275
02:27:27,110 --> 02:27:29,940
- You're just the afterbirth, Eli. - No.

1276
02:27:30,050 --> 02:27:33,670
That slithered out on your mother's filth.

1277
02:27:33,810 --> 02:27:35,150
No.

1278
02:27:35,250 --> 02:27:39,450
They should've put you in a glass jar on the mantelpiece.

1279
02:27:41,160 --> 02:27:44,520
Where were you when Paul was suckling at his mother's teat?

1280
02:27:44,660 --> 02:27:46,150
Where were you?

1281
02:27:46,290 --> 02:27:50,990
Who was nursing you, poor Eli? One of Bandy's sows?

1282
02:27:51,130 --> 02:27:54,070
That land has been had. Nothing you can do about it. It's gone.

1283
02:27:54,170 --> 02:27:56,330
- lf you would just take this lease... - You lose.

1284
02:27:56,470 --> 02:27:59,700
Drainage!

1285
02:28:00,740 --> 02:28:04,300
Drainage, Eli, you boy.

1286
02:28:05,450 --> 02:28:08,350
Drained dry. I'm so sorry.

1287
02:28:09,580 --> 02:28:11,680
If you have a milkshake

1288
02:28:12,790 --> 02:28:14,550
and I have a milkshake,

1289
02:28:14,660 --> 02:28:17,850
and I have a straw, there it is. That's the straw, you see?

1290
02:28:17,960 --> 02:28:19,520
Watch it.

1291
02:28:20,960 --> 02:28:27,890
Now my straw reaches across the room

1292
02:28:29,170 --> 02:28:31,970
and starts to drink your milkshake.

1293
02:28:32,910 --> 02:28:36,670
I drink your milkshake!

1294
02:28:38,880 --> 02:28:42,340
- I drink it up! - Don't bully me, Daniel.

1295
02:28:45,090 --> 02:28:50,290
Did you think your song and dance and your superstition would help you, Eli?

1296
02:28:50,420 --> 02:28:55,050
I am the Third Revelation. I am who the Lord has chosen.

1297
02:28:57,260 --> 02:28:59,560
- Daniel! - Because I'm smarter than you!

1298
02:28:59,670 --> 02:29:01,130
I'm older!

1299
02:29:01,970 --> 02:29:03,800
I'm your old friend, Daniel!

1300
02:29:03,900 --> 02:29:06,340
- I'm not a false prophet... - Help me! Help me!

1301
02:29:06,440 --> 02:29:08,700
...you sniveling boy!

1302
02:29:08,810 --> 02:29:15,480
I am the Third Revelation! I am the Third Revelation!

1303
02:29:15,580 --> 02:29:18,550
- I told you I would eat you. - We're family!

1304
02:29:18,690 --> 02:29:23,120
- I told you I would eat you up! - We're brothers! We're brothers!

1305
02:29:30,230 --> 02:29:33,030
Daniel, please forgive me. I beg you.

1306
02:29:36,700 --> 02:29:38,760
That's it. That's it.

1307
02:30:41,170 --> 02:30:42,640
Mr. Daniel?

1308
02:30:50,540 --> 02:30:52,210
I'm finished.

